window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-820e54e1b31b71d3"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"developer-commands\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">开发者命令</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取文档页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT 网页版有自己的输入框命令菜单。输入 <code>/</code> 可查看当前聊天中 可用的操作。这里不会显示 ChatGPT 桌面应用或 CLI 的命令集； 本参考中的 Codex 斜杠命令、CLI 命令和标志 不适用于 ChatGPT 网页版。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"chatgpt-desktop-app-commands\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"chatgpt\">ChatGPT 桌面应用命令</h2> <p>通用<a href=\"#/article/a-dd7bb821828a3c32\">命令</a>页面介绍了应用导航、 聊天快捷方式、键盘自定义，以及指向聊天、设置、 技能、计划任务、插件和宠物的深层链接。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-6c3aed9dab628df5\">斜杠命令</a>页面介绍了 应用输入框中可用的命令，包括 <code>/feedback</code>、<code>/goal</code>、<code>/init</code>、 <code>/mcp</code>、<code>/plan</code>、<code>/review</code> 和 <code>/status</code>。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"how-to-read-this-reference\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">如何阅读本参考文档</h2> <p>本页汇总了所有有文档说明的 Codex CLI 命令和标志。官网交互式表格可按键或说明搜索。各部分会显示选项的成熟度，并标示已弃用选项及有风险的组合。</p> <blockquote> <p>本地版说明：本地译本将官网交互式表格展开为静态表格；请使用浏览器的“在页面上查找”（通常按 Ctrl+F）检索。</p> </blockquote> <p>CLI 会从 <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code> 继承大多数默认值。任何 在命令行传入的 <code>-c key=value</code> 覆盖项 只对本次调用生效。更多说明请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76?anchor=configuration-precedence\">配置 基础</a>，了解更多 信息。</p> <p><a id=\"global-flags\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">全局标志</h2> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>globalFlagOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>这些选项适用于基础 <code>codex</code> 命令。大多数选项也会传递给子命令； 例外情况请查看上文备注或对应命令的帮助信息。对于会传递的 标志，请以对应命令的帮助说明为准。例如，<code>codex exec --oss ...</code> 会将 <code>--oss</code> 应用于 <code>exec</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"command-overview\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">命令概览</h2> <p>“成熟度”列会使用 Experimental（实验性）、Beta（测试版）、 Stable（稳定版）和 Deprecated（已弃用）等功能成熟度标签。有关这些标签的 含义，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d303113c34a6b1a9\">功能成熟度</a>。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>commandOverview</code></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"command-details\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">命令详解</h2> <p><a id=\"codex-interactive\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex\"><code>codex</code>（交互模式）</h3> <p>不带子命令运行 <code>codex</code> 会启动交互式终端界面（TUI）。该智能体接受上文所列的全局标志，也支持附加图像。网页搜索默认使用缓存模式；添加 <code>--search</code> 可切换为实时搜索。若要简化本地任务的操作，请使用 <code>--sandbox workspace-write --ask-for-approval on-request</code>。</p> <p>使用 <code>--remote ws://host:port</code> 或 <code>--remote wss://host:port</code>，将 TUI 连接到通过 <code>codex app-server --listen ws://IP:PORT</code> 启动的应用服务器。连接本地 Unix 套接字时，使用 <code>--remote unix://</code> 指定默认套接字，或使用 <code>--remote unix://PATH</code> 指定具体路径。如果服务器要求通过 bearer token 进行 WebSocket 身份验证，请添加 <code>--remote-auth-token-env &lt;ENV_VAR&gt;</code>。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-agents\"><code>codex agents</code>（智能体命令中心）</h3> <p>在共享服务器上打开聊天命令中心，以浏览聊天并在智能体之间切换。使用 <code>--remote &lt;URL&gt;</code> 连接远程服务器，使用 <code>--cd &lt;DIR&gt;</code> 设置新远程任务的目录。<code>codex agents</code> 不支持 <code>--no-daemon</code>。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-queue\"><code>codex queue</code>（向现有会话排队发送消息）</h3> <p>为现有会话排入一条文本消息：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex queue --thread &lt;SESSION_ID&gt; --message \"Run the remaining checks\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>--thread</code> 接受 UUID 或精确会话名称。如果有多个会话同名，请使用 UUID。此命令还接受 <code>--remote</code> 和 <code>--remote-auth-token-env</code>；不支持附加图像。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-app-server\"><code>codex app-server</code>（应用服务器）</h3> <p>在本地启动 Codex 应用服务器。此功能主要用于开发和调试，可能会随时变更，恕不另行通知。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>appServerOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>codex app-server --listen stdio://</code> 保持默认的标准输入/输出 JSONL 传输行为；<code>codex app-server --stdio</code> 是该传输方式的别名。<code>--listen ws://IP:PORT</code> 会为 app-server 客户端启用 WebSocket 传输。服务器接受 <code>ws://</code> 监听 URL；客户端通过 <code>wss://</code> 连接时，请使用 TLS 终止或安全代理。使用 <code>--listen unix://</code> 可在 Codex 默认 Unix 套接字上接受 WebSocket 握手；使用 <code>--listen unix:///absolute/path.sock</code> 可指定套接字路径。若要为客户端绑定生成架构，请添加 <code>--experimental</code>，以包含受功能开关限制的字段和方法。</p> <p>添加 <code>--code-mode-host wss://code-mode.example.com/host</code>，将 app-server 连接到 远程 Code Mode 主机，而不是启动本地主机。此出站 连接独立于 <code>--listen</code>，并由该进程中的所有线程共用。 仅当主机位于本地或通过 SSH 转发时才使用 <code>ws://</code>。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-remote-control\"><code>codex remote-control</code>（远程控制）</h3> <p>运行 <code>codex remote-control</code>，通过受管后台服务器启动远程控制（符合条件时）；若不符合条件，则退回前台运行。使用 <code>codex remote-control --no-daemon</code> 可明确要求在前台运行。使用 <code>codex remote-control start</code> 启动启用了远程控制的本地 app-server 守护进程，使用 <code>codex remote-control stop</code> 停止该进程。托管的 远程控制客户端和 SSH 远程工作流会使用这些命令；但在构建本地协议客户端时，这些命令不能替代 <code>codex app-server --listen</code>。</p> <p>守护进程启动后，运行 <code>codex remote-control pair</code> 创建并 打印一个短时有效的手动配对码。为任意远程控制 命令添加 <code>--json</code>，即可获取机器可读的输出。对于 <code>pair</code>，JSON 响应包含 <code>pairingCode</code>、<code>manualPairingCode</code>、<code>environmentId</code> 和 <code>expiresAt</code>。 <code>--no-daemon</code> 只适用于不带子命令的 <code>remote-control</code>；不要将其与 <code>start</code>、<code>stop</code> 或 <code>pair</code> 同时使用。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-app\"><code>codex app</code>（桌面应用）</h3> <p>在 macOS 或 Windows 上通过终端启动 ChatGPT 桌面应用。在 macOS 上， Codex 可以打开指定的工作区路径；在 Windows 上，Codex 会打印要打开的路径 以供打开。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>appOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>如果 ChatGPT 桌面应用已安装，运行 <code>codex app</code> 会将其打开；如果 应用尚未安装，则会启动安装程序。在 macOS 上，Codex 会打开指定的工作区路径；在 Windows 上，则会在安装后打印要打开的路径。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-debug-app-server-send-message-v2\"><code>codex debug app-server send-message-v2</code>（调试应用服务器消息接口）</h3> <p>使用内置的 app-server 测试客户端，通过 app-server 的 V2 线程/轮次流程发送一条消息。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>debugAppServerSendMessageV2Options</code></p> </blockquote> <p>此调试流程会以 <code>experimentalApi: true</code> 初始化，启动线程、发送一轮请求并流式接收服务器通知。你可以用它在本地复现并检查 app-server 协议行为。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-debug-models\"><code>codex debug models</code>（调试模型）</h3> <p>将 Codex 读取到的原始模型目录以 JSON 格式打印出来。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>debugModelsOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>如果只想检查当前二进制文件随附的模型目录，而不从远程模型端点刷新，请使用 <code>--bundled</code>。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-debug-prompt-input\"><code>codex debug prompt-input</code>（调试提示词输入）</h3> <p>将模型实际可见的提示词输入列表原样输出为 JSON。以下情况可使用此命令： 排查指令发现、会话上下文或提示词构建问题。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>debugPromptInputOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-apply\"><code>codex apply</code>（应用更改）</h3> <p>将 Codex 云端聊天中最近一次的差异应用到本地代码库。你必须先完成身份验证，并且拥有访问该聊天的权限。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>applyOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>如果 <code>git apply</code> 失败（例如发生冲突），Codex 会打印已修补的文件，并以非零状态码退出。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-review\"><code>codex review</code>（审查更改）</h3> <p>以非交互方式执行代码审查。请选择且只选择一个审查目标，或将 自定义审查说明作为提示词传入。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>reviewOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>--uncommitted</code>、<code>--base</code>、<code>--commit</code> 和自定义 <code>PROMPT</code> 彼此 冲突。<code>--title</code> 只能与 <code>--commit</code> 一起使用。</p> <p><a id=\"codex-archive-and-codex-unarchive\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex-archive-codex-unarchive\"><code>codex archive</code> 与 <code>codex unarchive</code>（归档与取消归档）</h3> <p>按会话 ID 或会话名称归档或恢复已保存的交互式会话。 如果想整理会话选择器但不删除聊天记录，请使用这些命令。会话 ID 的优先级高于会话名称。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex archive &lt;SESSION&gt;\ncodex unarchive &lt;SESSION&gt;\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>archiveOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-delete\"><code>codex delete</code>（删除会话）</h3> <p>按会话 ID 或会话名称永久删除已保存的交互式会话。 只有在确实要删除聊天记录，而不是将其从 活动会话列表中隐藏时，才使用此命令。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex delete &lt;SESSION&gt;\ncodex delete &lt;SESSION_UUID&gt; --force\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>deleteOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>只有在提供会话 UUID 时才使用 <code>--force</code>。对于命名会话，仍然需要 确认操作，避免 Codex 在没有提示的情况下删除重名或含义不明确的会话。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-cloud\"><code>codex cloud</code>（云端）</h3> <p>在终端中与 Codex 云端聊天交互。默认命令会打开交互式选择器；<code>codex cloud exec</code> 可直接提交任务，而 <code>codex cloud list</code> 会返回最近的聊天，供脚本处理或快速查看。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>cloudExecOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>身份验证使用与主 CLI 相同的凭据。如果任务提交失败，Codex 会以非零状态码退出。</p> <h4 id=\"codex-cloud-list\"><code>codex cloud list</code>（列出云端任务）</h4> <p>列出最近的云端聊天，并支持筛选和分页。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>cloudListOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>纯文本输出会先打印任务 URL，随后显示状态详情。自动化场景请使用 <code>--json</code>。JSON 负载包含 <code>tasks</code> 数组和可选的 <code>cursor</code> 值。每个任务包含 <code>id</code>、<code>url</code>、<code>title</code>、<code>status</code>、<code>updated_at</code>、<code>environment_id</code>、<code>environment_label</code>、<code>summary</code>、<code>is_review</code> 和 <code>attempt_total</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"codex-completion\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex-completionshell\"><code>codex completion</code>（Shell 命令补全）</h3> <p>生成 Shell 补全脚本，并将输出重定向到适当位置，例如 <code>codex completion zsh &gt; \"${fpath[1]}/_codex\"</code>。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>completionOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-doctor\"><code>codex doctor</code>（诊断）</h3> <p>提交支持请求之前，或 排查 Codex 安装故障时，生成本地诊断报告。该报告会检查安装、 配置、身份验证、运行时、Git、终端、app-server 以及线程 清单的健康状态。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>doctorOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-features\"><code>codex features</code>（功能开关）</h3> <p>管理存储在 <code>$CODEX_HOME/config.toml</code> 中的功能标志。<code>enable</code> 和 <code>disable</code> 命令会保存更改，使其在后续会话中继续生效。 <code>features</code> 子命令不接受 <code>--profile</code>。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>featuresOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-exec\"><code>codex exec</code>（执行任务）</h3> <p>对于应当无需人工交互即可完成的脚本任务或 CI 运行，请使用 <code>codex exec</code>（或简写 <code>codex e</code>）。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>execOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>Codex 默认输出格式化文本。添加 <code>--json</code> 可接收按行分隔的 JSON 事件（每次状态变更对应一个事件）。可选的 <code>resume</code> 子命令可继续非交互式任务。使用 <code>--last</code> 选择当前工作目录中最近的会话，或添加 <code>--all</code> 搜索所有会话：</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>execResumeOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>使用 <code>codex exec fork &lt;SESSION_ID&gt; [PROMPT]</code> 可将已保存的会话复制到一个新会话中。会话参数接受 UUID 或名称。不提供提示时，Codex 会创建分叉会话但不会启动新一轮对话。将 <code>-</code> 作为提示可从标准输入读取提示；也可以添加 <code>--image</code> 附加图像。</p> <p>使用图像、<code>--output-schema</code>、<code>--output-last-message</code> 或 <code>--ephemeral</code> 时，必须提供提示。</p> <p>为新的运行或分叉出的运行添加 <code>--worktree</code>，即可创建受管 Git 工作树：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex exec --worktree \"implement the next step\"\ncodex exec fork &lt;SESSION_ID&gt; --worktree \"try an alternative approach\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>--worktree</code> 需要本地执行。不能与 <code>resume</code>、<code>review</code>、<code>--ephemeral</code> 或 <code>--ignore-user-config</code> 同时使用。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-execpolicy\"><code>codex execpolicy</code>（执行策略）</h3> <p>保存 <code>execpolicy</code> 规则文件之前，请先检查。<code>codex execpolicy check</code> 接受一个或多个 <code>--rules</code> 标志（例如 <code>~/.codex/rules</code> 目录中的文件），并输出 JSON，显示最严格的判定和任何匹配规则。添加 <code>--pretty</code> 可格式化输出。<code>execpolicy</code> 命令目前处于预览阶段。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>execpolicyOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-login\"><code>codex login</code>（登录）</h3> <p>使用 ChatGPT 账户、API 密钥或访问令牌对 CLI 进行身份验证。不带标志时，Codex 会打开浏览器，启动 ChatGPT OAuth 流程。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>loginOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>存在凭据时，<code>codex login status</code> 会以 <code>0</code> 退出，因此适合用于自动化脚本。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-logout\"><code>codex logout</code>（退出登录）</h3> <p>删除 API 密钥和 ChatGPT 身份验证所保存的凭据。此命令不接受任何标志。</p> <p><a id=\"codex-mcp\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex-mcpmcp\"><code>codex mcp</code>（MCP 服务）</h3> <p>管理保存在 <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code> 中的模型上下文协议（MCP）服务器条目。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>mcpCommands</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>add</code> 子命令同时支持 stdio 和流式 HTTP 传输：</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>mcpAddOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>OAuth 操作（<code>login</code>、<code>logout</code>）仅适用于支持流式 HTTP 传输的服务器，且服务器本身必须支持 OAuth。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-plugin\"><code>codex plugin</code>（插件）</h3> <p>从已配置的市场安装、列出和移除插件。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>pluginCommands</code></p> </blockquote> <p>运行 <code>codex plugin add --json</code> 会输出 <code>pluginId</code>、<code>name</code>、<code>marketplaceName</code>、 <code>version</code>、<code>installedPath</code> 和 <code>authPolicy</code>。运行 <code>codex plugin list --json</code> 会输出 <code>installed</code> 和 <code>available</code> 数组。每个条目包含 <code>pluginId</code>、<code>name</code>、 <code>marketplaceName</code>、<code>version</code>、<code>installed</code>、<code>enabled</code>、<code>source</code> 和 <code>installPolicy</code>、 <code>authPolicy</code>；如果存在 <code>marketplaceSource</code>，还会包含已配置的 市场来源类型和值。运行 <code>codex plugin remove --json</code> 会输出 <code>pluginId</code>、<code>name</code> 和 <code>marketplaceName</code>。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-plugin-marketplace\"><code>codex plugin marketplace</code>（插件市场）</h3> <p>管理 Codex 可浏览并用于安装插件的市场来源。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>marketplaceCommands</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>codex plugin marketplace add</code> 支持 GitHub 简写形式，例如 <code>owner/repo</code> 或 <code>owner/repo@ref</code>、HTTP/HTTPS Git URL、SSH Git URL，以及本地市场 根目录。使用 <code>--ref</code> 固定 Git 引用；对于基于 Git 的市场仓库，可重复指定 <code>--sparse PATH</code> 以进行稀疏检出。</p> <p><code>codex plugin marketplace list</code> 会显示当前范围内的市场名称和根目录， 包括自动发现的默认市场，以及已配置市场的 快照。</p> <p>为市场添加、列出、升级或移除命令添加 <code>--json</code>，以获得 便于自动化处理的输出。添加市场时，JSON 包含 <code>marketplaceName</code>、 <code>installedRoot</code> 和 <code>alreadyAdded</code>；列出市场时，JSON 包含 <code>marketplaces</code> 数组， 其中有 <code>name</code>、<code>root</code>，以及可选的 <code>marketplaceSource</code>；升级时，JSON 包含 <code>selectedMarketplaces</code>、<code>upgradedRoots</code> 和 <code>errors</code>；移除时，JSON 包含 <code>marketplaceName</code> 和 <code>installedRoot</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"codex-mcp-server\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex-mcp-servermcp\"><code>codex mcp-server</code>（MCP 服务器）</h3> <p><code>codex mcp-server</code> 命令和独立的 <code>codex-mcp-server</code> 二进制文件已经 移除。请改用 <a href=\"#/article/a-341246db376ea9e1\">Codex 应用服务器</a>。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-resume\"><code>codex resume</code>（恢复会话）</h3> <p>按 ID 继续交互式会话，或恢复最近的聊天。<code>codex resume</code> 默认将 <code>--last</code> 限定在当前工作目录中，除非你传入 <code>--all</code>。该命令接受模型和沙箱覆盖设置，但不接受 <code>--worktree</code>。</p> <p>如果当前工作目录与会话保存的目录不同， Codex 会询问要使用哪个目录。将 <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\"><code>tui.resume_cwd</code></a> 设置为 <code>\"current\"</code> 或 <code>\"session\"</code>，即可不经提示地沿用该选择。显式指定 <code>--cd</code>（<code>-C</code>） 时，其优先级高于 <code>tui.resume_cwd</code>。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>resumeOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-fork\"><code>codex fork</code>（分叉会话）</h3> <p>将之前的交互式会话分叉为新聊天。默认情况下，<code>codex fork</code> 会打开会话选择器；添加 <code>--last</code> 可改为分叉最近的会话。</p> <p>如果当前目录与会话保存的目录不同，<code>codex fork</code> 会使用与 <code>codex resume</code> 相同的工作目录提示和 <code>tui.resume_cwd</code> 设置。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>forkOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>若要在受管 Git 工作树中分叉，请运行 <code>codex fork &lt;SESSION_ID&gt; --worktree</code>。此操作需要明确指定会话 ID 并在本地执行；不支持 <code>--last</code> 或会话选择器。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-sandbox\"><code>codex sandbox</code>（沙箱）</h3> <p>使用沙箱辅助命令，以 Codex 内部相同的策略运行命令。</p> <h4 id=\"macos-seatbelt\">macOS Seatbelt 沙箱</h4> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>sandboxMacOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"linux-landlock\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"linux-sandbox\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"linux\">Linux 沙箱</h4> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>sandboxLinuxOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h4 id=\"windows\">Windows 环境</h4> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>sandboxWindowsOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-update\"><code>codex update</code>（更新）</h3> <p>如果已安装的版本支持自我更新，可检查并安装 Codex CLI 更新。调试版会提示你改为安装正式发行版。</p> <p><a id=\"flag-combinations-and-safety-tips\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">标志组合与安全提示</h2> <ul> <li>对可限制在工作区内的无人值守本地任务，请使用 <code>--sandbox workspace-write</code>；除非处于专用沙箱虚拟机中，否则不要使用 <code>--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox</code>。</li> <li>需要允许 Codex 写入更多目录时，优先使用 <code>--add-dir</code>，不要强行启用 <code>--sandbox danger-full-access</code>。</li> <li>在 CI 中同时使用 <code>--json</code> 和 <code>--output-last-message</code>，即可记录机器可读的执行进度以及最终的自然语言摘要。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"interactive-shortcuts\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">交互快捷操作</h2> <ul> <li>输入 <code>@</code> 搜索工作区中的文件，并将文件路径添加到提示词中。</li> <li>按 <kbd>Up</kbd> 或 <kbd>Down</kbd> 可调出草稿历史记录。</li> <li>按 <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>R</kbd> 搜索提示词历史记录；找到匹配项后按 <kbd>Enter</kbd> 使用，或按 <kbd>Escape</kbd> 取消。</li> <li>按 <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>O</kbd>，或运行 <code>/copy</code>，即可复制 Codex 最近一次已完成的输出。</li> <li>在一行命令前加上 <code>!</code>，即可按照当前审批和沙箱设置运行本地 Shell 命令。</li> <li>Codex 正在工作时按 <kbd>Tab</kbd>，可将后续提示词、斜杠命令或 Shell 命令排入下一轮。</li> <li>Codex 正在工作时按 <kbd>Enter</kbd>，可将新指令追加到当前轮次。</li> <li>输入框为空时连续按两次 <kbd>Escape</kbd>，即可编辑上一条用户消息，并从该处分叉出新的聊天。</li> <li>按 <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>C</kbd>，或运行 <code>/exit</code>，即可结束会话。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"related-resources\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">相关资源</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d\">Codex CLI 概览</a>：了解安装、升级和实用技巧。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">配置基础</a>：保存模型、提供方等默认设置。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85\">高级配置</a>：配置档案、提供方、沙箱调优和集成。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-94f17e3de1ca7cb3\">AGENTS.md 指南</a>：了解 Codex 智能体的能力概念与最佳实践。</li> </ul> <p>斜杠命令让你优先使用键盘快速控制 Codex。在 输入框中输入 <code>/</code> 打开斜杠命令菜单，选择命令后，Codex 会执行 切换模型、调整权限或总结较长 聊天等操作，无需离开终端。</p> <p>本指南将介绍如何：</p> <ul> <li>为当前任务查找合适的内置斜杠命令。</li> <li>使用 <code>/model</code>、<code>/fast</code>、<code>/permissions</code>、<code>/approve</code>、<code>/raw</code>、<code>/agents</code>、<code>/subagents</code> 和 <code>/status</code> 等命令调整当前会话。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"built-in-slash-commands\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">内置斜杠命令</h2> <p>Codex 内置了以下命令。打开斜杠命令菜单并开始输入 命令名称即可筛选列表。</p> <p>聊天正在运行时，你可以输入斜杠命令并按 <code>Tab</code>，将它 排入下一轮。Codex 会在执行时解析排队的斜杠命令，因此 命令菜单和错误会在当前轮次结束后显示。斜杠命令 的自动补全功能在命令排队前仍然可用。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>命令</th> <th>用途</th> <th>适用场景</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=update-permissions-with-permissions\"><code>/permissions</code></a></td> <td>设置 Codex 无需事先询问即可执行的操作。</td> <td>在会话进行中放宽或收紧审批要求，例如在 Auto 和 Read Only 之间切换。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=include-ide-context-with-ide\"><code>/ide</code></a></td> <td>纳入已打开的文件、当前选区及其他 IDE 上下文。</td> <td>将编辑器上下文带入下一条提示词，无需再次说明 IDE 中打开了哪些内容。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=remap-tui-shortcuts-with-keymap\"><code>/keymap</code></a></td> <td>重新映射 TUI 键盘快捷键。</td> <td>检查自定义快捷键绑定，并将其保存到 <code>config.toml</code>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=toggle-vim-mode-with-vim\"><code>/vim</code></a></td> <td>切换输入框的 Vim 模式。</td> <td>在 Vim 普通/插入模式和默认输入框编辑模式之间切换。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=set-up-the-elevated-windows-sandbox-with-setup-default-sandbox\"><code>/setup-default-sandbox</code></a></td> <td>设置提升权限的智能体沙箱（仅限 Windows）。</td> <td>Codex 提供提升权限设置后，用该设置替换降级的 Windows 沙箱。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=manage-chats-with-agents\"><code>/agents</code></a></td> <td>打开智能体命令中心。</td> <td>浏览聊天，并在已连接的服务器上切换智能体。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=switch-agent-threads-with-subagents\"><code>/subagents</code></a></td> <td>切换当前活动的子智能体线程。</td> <td>查看或继续处理当前会话中的子智能体。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=browse-apps-with-apps\"><code>/apps</code></a></td> <td>浏览应用（连接器），并将其插入提示词。</td> <td>要求 Codex 使用应用前，先将其作为 <code>$app-slug</code> 附加到提示词中。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=browse-plugins-with-plugins\"><code>/plugins</code></a></td> <td>浏览已安装和可发现的插件。</td> <td>检查插件工具、安装建议的插件，或管理插件的可用状态。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=view-and-manage-lifecycle-hooks-with-hooks\"><code>/hooks</code></a></td> <td>查看和管理生命周期钩子。</td> <td>检查已配置的钩子、信任新增或已更改的钩子，或在非托管钩子运行前将其停用。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=clear-the-terminal-and-start-a-new-chat-with-clear\"><code>/clear</code></a></td> <td>清空终端并开始新的聊天。</td> <td>想要重新开始时，同时重置可见界面和聊天上下文。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=rename-the-current-chat-with-rename\"><code>/rename</code></a></td> <td>重命名当前聊天。</td> <td>无需离开 TUI，即可为已保存的会话设置一个易于识别的名称。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=archive-the-current-session-with-archive\"><code>/archive</code></a></td> <td>归档当前会话。</td> <td>将当前会话从活动会话列表中移除，但不删除聊天记录。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=delete-the-current-session-with-delete\"><code>/delete</code></a></td> <td>永久删除当前会话。</td> <td>归档无法满足需求时，删除聊天记录及其派生会话。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=keep-transcripts-lean-with-compact\"><code>/compact</code></a></td> <td>总结当前可见聊天，以释放令牌上下文空间。</td> <td>长时间运行后可使用此命令，让 Codex 保留要点而不耗尽上下文窗口。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=copy-the-latest-response-with-copy\"><code>/copy</code></a></td> <td>复制 Codex 最近一次已完成的输出。</td> <td>无需手动选择，即可复制最近完成的回复或计划文本。也可以按 <code>Ctrl+O</code>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=review-changes-with-diff\"><code>/diff</code></a></td> <td>显示 Git 差异，包括 Git 尚未跟踪的文件。</td> <td>提交或运行测试前，检查 Codex 所做的修改。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=exit-the-cli-with-quit-or-exit\"><code>/exit</code></a></td> <td>退出 CLI（与 <code>/quit</code> 相同）。</td> <td>这是另一种拼写；两个命令都会退出会话。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=toggle-experimental-features-with-experimental\"><code>/experimental</code></a></td> <td>切换实验性功能。</td> <td>启用 Network proxy（网络代理）或 Prevent sleep while running（运行时防止休眠）等选项。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=approve-an-auto-review-denial-with-approve\"><code>/approve</code></a></td> <td>批准对最近一次自动审查拒绝的操作重试一次。</td> <td>重试自动审查器拒绝的命令或操作。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=configure-memories-with-memories\"><code>/memories</code></a></td> <td>配置记忆的使用和生成方式。</td> <td>无需离开 TUI，即可开启或关闭记忆注入或记忆生成功能。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=use-skills-with-skills\"><code>/skills</code></a></td> <td>浏览并使用技能。</td> <td>选择合适的本地技能，改进针对特定任务的行为。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=import-claude-code-or-cursor-setup-with-import\"><code>/import</code></a></td> <td>导入 Claude Code 或 Cursor 的设置、项目和聊天。</td> <td>将受支持的外部智能体资料迁移到 Codex 配置和本地文件中。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=send-feedback-with-feedback\"><code>/feedback</code></a></td> <td>向 Codex 维护人员发送日志。</td> <td>报告问题，或向支持团队提供诊断信息。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=generate-agentsmd-with-init\"><code>/init</code></a></td> <td>在当前目录生成 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 初始模板。</td> <td>为当前工作的代码库或子目录保存持久化指令。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=sign-out-with-logout\"><code>/logout</code></a></td> <td>退出 Codex 账户。</td> <td>在共用计算机上使用后，清除本地凭据。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=list-mcp-tools-with-mcp\"><code>/mcp</code></a></td> <td>列出已配置的模型上下文协议（MCP）工具。</td> <td>查看 Codex 在本会话中可以调用哪些外部工具；添加 <code>verbose</code> 可查看服务器详情。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=highlight-files-with-mention\"><code>/mention</code></a></td> <td>将文件附加到聊天中。</td> <td>指定希望 Codex 接下来检查的文件或文件夹。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=set-the-active-model-with-model\"><code>/model</code></a></td> <td>选择当前模型（以及可用时的推理强度）。</td> <td>如果列表中显示 <code>gpt-6-luna</code> 或 <code>gpt-6.1-sol</code>，可选择其中之一。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=toggle-fast-mode-with-fast\"><code>/fast</code></a></td> <td>当模型目录提供 Fast 服务档位时，切换该档位。</td> <td>为当前模型启用或关闭 Fast 档位，并保存此选择。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=switch-to-plan-mode-with-plan\"><code>/plan</code></a></td> <td>切换到计划模式，也可以同时发送提示词。</td> <td>在开始实施前，让 Codex 先提出执行计划。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=set-or-view-a-task-goal-with-goal\"><code>/goal</code></a></td> <td>设置、编辑、暂停、恢复、查看或清除任务目标。</td> <td>为 Codex 设置一个持续目标，供它在执行较大任务时跟踪。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=check-background-terminals-with-ps\"><code>/ps</code></a></td> <td>显示后台终端及其最近的输出。</td> <td>无需离开主聊天记录，即可检查长时间运行的命令。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=stop-background-terminals-with-stop\"><code>/stop</code></a></td> <td>停止所有后台终端。</td> <td>取消当前会话启动的后台终端任务。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=fork-the-current-chat-with-fork\"><code>/fork</code></a></td> <td>将当前聊天分叉为一段新聊天。</td> <td>从当前会话分出新分支以尝试其他方案，同时保留现有聊天记录。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=continue-in-the-desktop-app-with-app\"><code>/app</code></a></td> <td>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中继续当前会话。</td> <td>在 macOS 或 Windows 上从 TUI 切换到桌面应用。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=start-a-side-chat-with-side\"><code>/side</code>, <code>/btw</code></a></td> <td>开始临时侧边聊天。</td> <td>在不干扰主聊天记录的情况下，专注处理一个后续问题。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=toggle-raw-scrollback-with-raw\"><code>/raw</code></a></td> <td>切换原始滚屏模式。</td> <td>查看长输出时，减少终端选取和复制内容中的格式处理。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=resume-a-saved-chat-with-resume\"><code>/resume</code></a></td> <td>从会话列表恢复已保存的聊天。</td> <td>无需从头开始，即可继续之前 CLI 会话中的工作。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=start-a-new-chat-with-new\"><code>/new</code></a></td> <td>在同一个 CLI 会话中开始新的聊天。</td> <td>想在同一代码库中使用新的提示词时，可在不退出 CLI 的情况下重置聊天上下文。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=exit-the-cli-with-quit-or-exit\"><code>/quit</code></a></td> <td>退出 CLI。</td> <td>立即退出会话。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=ask-for-a-working-tree-review-with-review\"><code>/review</code></a></td> <td>让 Codex 检查你的工作树。</td> <td>Codex 完成工作后，或你想让它再次检查本地更改时运行。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=inspect-the-session-with-status\"><code>/status</code></a></td> <td>显示会话配置和令牌用量。</td> <td>确认当前模型、审批策略、可写入根目录以及剩余上下文容量。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=view-account-usage-with-usage\"><code>/usage</code></a></td> <td>查看账户令牌用量，或使用速率限制重置次数。</td> <td>在 TUI 中查看 ChatGPT 令牌的每日、每周或累计活动。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=inspect-config-layers-with-debug-config\"><code>/debug-config</code></a></td> <td>打印配置层级和要求诊断信息。</td> <td>排查优先级和策略要求，包括实验性网络限制。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=configure-footer-items-with-statusline\"><code>/statusline</code></a></td> <td>以交互方式配置 TUI 状态行字段。</td> <td>选择并重新排列页脚项目（模型/上下文/限制/Git/令牌/会话），并将设置保存到 config.toml。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=configure-terminal-title-items-with-title\"><code>/title</code></a></td> <td>以交互方式配置终端窗口或标签页标题字段。</td> <td>选择并重新排列标题项目，例如项目、状态、线程、分支、模型和任务进度。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=choose-a-syntax-theme-with-theme\"><code>/theme</code></a></td> <td>选择语法高亮主题。</td> <td>预览终端语法高亮主题并保存选择。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=choose-a-terminal-pet-with-pets\"><code>/pets</code>, <code>/pet</code></a></td> <td>选择或隐藏终端宠物。</td> <td>使用内置或自定义的伴随宠物个性化设置 TUI。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=choose-the-terminal-mode-with-tui\"><code>/tui</code></a></td> <td>选择下次启动时使用的终端模式。</td> <td>在终端滚屏与全屏聊天记录之间切换。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=export-a-conversation-with-export\"><code>/export</code></a></td> <td>将对话导出为 Markdown。</td> <td>将完整聊天记录保存到文件或复制到剪贴板。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=summarize-the-chat-with-recap\"><code>/recap</code></a></td> <td>生成当前对话的摘要。</td> <td>不压缩上下文，也能快速了解聊天内容。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=change-directories-with-cd\"><code>/cd</code></a></td> <td>更改会话的工作目录。</td> <td>让空闲的主聊天在另一个目录中继续。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=change-directories-with-cd\"><code>/pwd</code>, <code>/cwd</code></a></td> <td>显示工作目录。</td> <td>查看当前会话正在使用的目录。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=continue-in-a-worktree-with-worktree\"><code>/worktree</code></a></td> <td>在受管 Git 工作树中开始或继续聊天。</td> <td>在本地仓库的独立检出目录中工作。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=manage-the-background-server-with-daemon\"><code>/daemon</code></a></td> <td>打开后台服务器控制项。</td> <td>检查连接并管理由 Codex 管理的本地服务器。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=inspect-warnings-with-warnings\"><code>/warnings</code></a></td> <td>查看保留的警告和诊断信息。</td> <td>回看会话期间出现过的警告。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><code>/quit</code> 和 <code>/exit</code> 都会退出 CLI。请先保存或提交 所有重要工作，然后再使用它们。</p> <p>使用 <code>/permissions</code> 调整 Codex 无需事先询问即可执行的操作。 仅在需要重试自动审查器最近拒绝的操作时，才使用 <code>/approve</code> 。</p> <p><a id=\"control-your-session-with-slash-commands\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">使用斜杠命令控制会话</h2> <p>以下工作流可帮助你保持会话进度，无需重启 Codex。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-the-terminal-mode-with-tui\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"tui\">使用 <code>/tui</code> 选择终端模式</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/tui</code>。</li> <li>选择滚屏模式或全屏模式，然后确认。</li> <li>重启 Codex 以应用选择。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：下次启动时将使用已保存的终端模式。<code>--no-alt-screen</code> 等启动时覆盖项仍然有效。</p> <p><a id=\"export-a-conversation-with-export\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"export\">使用 <code>/export</code> 导出对话</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/export</code>。</li> <li>选择 <strong>复制到剪贴板</strong> 或 <strong>保存到文件</strong>。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会将完整对话导出为 Markdown。若要直接保存到文件，可运行 <code>/export session.md</code>。导出前请等待当前轮次完成。</p> <p><a id=\"summarize-the-chat-with-recap\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"recap\">使用 <code>/recap</code> 总结聊天</h3> <ol> <li>在 Codex 空闲时输入 <code>/recap</code>。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：即使 <code>tui.auto_recap = false</code>，Codex 也会生成对话摘要。若想释放上下文空间，请使用 <code>/compact</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"change-directories-with-cd\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"cd\">使用 <code>/cd</code> 更改目录</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/pwd</code>（或 <code>/cwd</code>）查看当前目录。</li> <li>输入 <code>/cd &lt;path&gt;</code> 更改目录；输入 <code>/cd</code> 则切换到主目录。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会在选定目录中继续当前聊天。更改目录要求主会话处于空闲状态，且没有排队的输入或后台终端。</p> <p><a id=\"continue-in-a-worktree-with-worktree\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"worktree\">使用 <code>/worktree</code> 在工作树中继续</h3> <ol> <li>在本地 Git 仓库中输入 <code>/worktree</code>。</li> <li>选择开始新聊天，或在新的工作树中继续当前对话。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会创建一个受管 Git 工作树，并在其中启动所选聊天。选择 <strong>浏览工作树</strong> 可查找已有工作树及其所属聊天。此命令需要本地工作树支持，且任务运行期间不可用。</p> <p><a id=\"manage-the-background-server-with-daemon\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"daemon\">使用 <code>/daemon</code> 管理后台服务器</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/daemon</code>。</li> <li>查看服务器连接状态和可用操作。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会提供将本地后台服务器更新到最新公开稳定版，或改用当前 CLI 构建版本的选项。确认更新会退出 Codex，并可能中断正在进行的工作。若连接的是远程服务器，请在其所在主机上管理服务器。</p> <p><a id=\"inspect-warnings-with-warnings\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"warnings\">使用 <code>/warnings</code> 查看警告</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/warnings</code>。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会显示保留的警告及其诊断详情。</p> <p><a id=\"set-the-active-model-with-model\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"model\">使用 <code>/model</code> 设置当前模型</h3> <p>选择器只会显示你的账户和工作区可用的模型。如果列表中没有 GPT-6.1 Sol，请选择其他模型。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6.1-sol\">各方案的 GPT-6.1 Sol 可用性</a>。</p> <ol> <li>启动 Codex 并打开输入框。</li> <li>输入 <code>/model</code>，然后按 Enter。</li> <li>从弹出窗口中选择一个模型，例如 <code>gpt-6-luna</code> 或 <code>gpt-6.1-sol</code>。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会在聊天记录中确认新模型。运行 <code>/status</code> 可核实更改。</p> <p><a id=\"toggle-fast-mode-with-fast\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"fast-fast-mode\">使用 <code>/fast</code> 切换 Fast mode</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/fast</code>，为当前模型启用 Fast 服务档位。</li> <li>再次输入 <code>/fast</code> 可将其关闭。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会切换服务档位并保存选择。你也可以在 TUI 页脚中 通过 <code>/statusline</code> 显示 Fast 模式状态项。</p> <p>Fast 服务档位命令由模型目录决定。如果当前模型没有声明支持 Fast 档位，Codex 就不会显示 <code>/fast</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"switch-to-plan-mode-with-plan\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"plan\">使用 <code>/plan</code> 切换到计划模式</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/plan</code>，然后按 Enter，将当前聊天切换到计划 模式。</li> <li>可选：附加内嵌提示词文本，例如 <code>/plan Propose a\nmigration plan for this service</code>).</li> <li>使用内嵌 <code>/plan</code> 参数时，也可以粘贴内容或附加图片。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会进入计划模式，并将你可选提供的内嵌提示词作为第一条规划请求。</p> <p>Codex 正在工作时，<code>/plan</code> 会暂时不可用。</p> <p><a id=\"set-or-view-a-task-goal-with-goal\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"goal\">使用 <code>/goal</code> 设置或查看任务目标</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/goal &lt;objective&gt;</code> 设置目标，例如 <code>/goal Finish the migration and keep tests green</code>。</li> <li>输入 <code>/goal</code> 查看当前目标。</li> <li>使用 <code>/goal edit</code> 修改目标；使用 <code>/goal pause</code> 暂停、<code>/goal resume</code> 恢复，或使用 <code>/goal clear</code> 清除目标。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：任务继续进行期间，Codex 会将目标保留在当前聊天中。</p> <p>目标内容不能为空，且最多为 4,000 个字符。如果说明更长， 请将详细内容写入文件，并让目标引用该文件。</p> <p><a id=\"toggle-experimental-features-with-experimental\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"experimental\">使用 <code>/experimental</code> 切换实验性功能</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/experimental</code>，然后按 Enter。</li> <li>开启或关闭所需功能（例如 Network proxy〔网络代理〕或 Prevent sleep while running〔运行时防止休眠〕）；如果出现提示，请重启 Codex。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会将你选择的功能保存到配置中，并在重启后应用。</p> <p><a id=\"approve-an-auto-review-denial-with-approve\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"approve\">使用 <code>/approve</code> 批准自动审查拒绝的操作</h3> <p>如果自动审查器最近拒绝了一项操作，而你希望 Codex 重试一次，请使用 <code>/approve</code>。</p> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/approve</code>。</li> <li>当 Codex 显示相应的被拒绝操作时，确认是否重试。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会根据当前会话策略，对被拒绝的操作重试一次 。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-memories-with-memories\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"memories\">使用 <code>/memories</code> 配置记忆</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/memories</code>。</li> <li>选择 Codex 应使用现有记忆、生成新记忆，还是 或保持记忆功能关闭。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会更新相关记忆设置，供后续会话使用。</p> <p><a id=\"use-skills-with-skills\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"skills\">使用 <code>/skills</code> 管理技能</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/skills</code>。</li> <li>选择要让 Codex 使用的技能。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会插入所选技能的上下文，使下一条请求遵循 该技能的指令。</p> <p><a id=\"import-claude-code-configuration-with-import\"></a> <a id=\"import-claude-code-setup-with-import\"></a> <a id=\"cli-import-claude-code-setup-with-import\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"import-claude-code-or-cursor-setup-with-import\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"import-claude-code-cursor\">使用 <code>/import</code> 导入 Claude Code 或 Cursor 配置</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/import</code>。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Claude Code</strong> 或 <strong>Cursor</strong>。</li> <li>选择要迁移的设置、项目文件或最近的聊天。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会打开外部智能体导入选择器，并导入所选的 受支持的内容，将其写入 Codex 配置和本地文件。会话发现功能 最多会列出过去 30 天内的 50 段聊天。</p> <p>请在本地 TUI 会话中运行 <code>/import</code>。任务运行期间、 远程会话中，以及连接到本地 app-server 守护进程时，都无法使用该命令。</p> <p>如需了解桌面应用中的导入流程和支持的内容类型，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-2b09a0f3c8670621\">从 其他智能体导入</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"clear-the-terminal-and-start-a-new-chat-with-clear\"></a> <a id=\"clear-the-terminal-and-start-a-new-task-with-clear\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"clear\">使用 <code>/clear</code> 清空终端并开始新聊天</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/clear</code>，然后按 Enter。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会清空终端、重置可见的聊天记录，并在同一 CLI 会话中 开始一段新的聊天。</p> <p>若要在创建新聊天时为其命名，请运行 <code>/clear release prep</code>。</p> <p>与 <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>L</kbd> 不同，<code>/clear</code> 会开始一段新聊天。</p> <p>按 <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>L</kbd> 只会清空终端视图，并保留当前 聊天内容。任务进行期间，Codex 会禁用这两项操作。</p> <p><a id=\"archive-the-current-session-with-archive\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"archive\">使用 <code>/archive</code> 归档当前会话</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/archive</code>，然后按 Enter。</li> <li>确认要归档当前会话。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：连接到本地后台服务器或远程服务器时，Codex 会归档会话并返回命令中心。若没有共享服务器，Codex 会退出。会话记录仍会保留；之后可使用 <code>codex unarchive &lt;SESSION&gt;</code> 将其恢复。</p> <p>如果某一轮仍在运行，确认 <code>/archive</code> 后 Codex 会先停止该轮，再归档会话。</p> <p><a id=\"delete-the-current-session-with-delete\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"delete\">使用 <code>/delete</code> 删除当前会话</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/delete</code>，然后按 Enter。</li> <li>确认要删除当前会话。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会永久删除会话记录及其派生的子会话。连接到本地后台服务器或远程服务器时，Codex 会返回命令中心；若没有共享服务器，Codex 会退出。</p> <p>聊天正在运行或处于侧边聊天中时，无法使用 <code>/delete</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"update-permissions-with-permissions\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"permissions\">使用 <code>/permissions</code> 更新权限</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/permissions</code>，然后按 Enter。</li> <li>选择符合你偏好的审批预设，例如 使用 <code>Auto</code> 进行无人干预的运行，或使用 <code>Read Only</code> 审查修改。启用命名 权限配置文件后，选择器还会显示已设置的自定义 配置文件及其说明。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会告知你策略已更新。之后的操作会遵循 更新后的审批模式，直到你再次更改为止。</p> <p><a id=\"include-ide-context-with-ide\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"ide-ide\">使用 <code>/ide</code> 加入 IDE 上下文</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/ide</code>。</li> <li>若要说明希望 Codex 对 当前 IDE 中选定的内容或已打开的文件执行什么操作，可以添加可选的内嵌文本。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会在下一条提示词中纳入可用的 IDE 上下文。</p> <p><a id=\"toggle-vim-mode-with-vim\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"vim-vim\">使用 <code>/vim</code> 切换 Vim 模式</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/vim</code>。</li> <li>继续在输入框中编辑。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会为当前会话切换输入框的 Vim 模式。若要让 Vim 模式成为新会话的默认设置，请在 <code>config.toml</code> 中设置 <code>tui.vim_mode_default = true</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"set-up-the-elevated-windows-sandbox-with-setup-default-sandbox\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"setup-default-sandbox-windows\">使用 <code>/setup-default-sandbox</code> 设置提升权限的 Windows 沙箱</h3> <p>仅当 Codex 在 Windows 上使用降级的 受限令牌沙箱时，才会显示此命令。</p> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/setup-default-sandbox</code>。</li> <li>按照管理员设置流程操作。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会配置提升权限的 Windows 沙箱，并选择 与之对应的自动审批预设。</p> <p><a id=\"copy-the-latest-response-with-copy\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"copy\">使用 <code>/copy</code> 复制最新响应</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/copy</code>，然后按 Enter。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会将 Codex 最近一次已完成的输出复制到剪贴板。</p> <p>如果当前轮次仍在运行，<code>/copy</code> 会复制最近一次已完成的输出，而不是 正在生成的回复。在 Codex 首次完成输出之前，以及 刚执行回滚后，此命令不可用。</p> <p>你也可以在主 TUI 中按 <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>O</kbd> 复制 最近一次已完成的回复，无需打开斜杠命令菜单。</p> <p><a id=\"toggle-raw-scrollback-with-raw\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"raw\">使用 <code>/raw</code> 切换原始滚屏模式</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/raw</code>、<code>/raw on</code> 或 <code>/raw off</code>。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会切换原始滚屏模式，让你更方便地选择和 复制终端内容。你也可以使用默认快捷键 <kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>R</kbd>， 或通过设置 <code>tui.raw_output_mode = true</code> 将其设为默认值。</p> <p><a id=\"inspect-the-session-with-status\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"status\">使用 <code>/status</code> 查看会话状态</h3> <ol> <li>在任意聊天中输入 <code>/status</code>。</li> <li>查看输出，确认当前模型、审批策略、可写入根目录以及 当前令牌用量。如果 TUI 通过远程方式连接，输出还会 显示远程地址和服务器版本。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会打印摘要，确认它正在你所 预期的环境中运行。</p> <p><a id=\"view-account-usage-with-usage\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"usage\">使用 <code>/usage</code> 查看账号用量</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/usage</code> 打开用量菜单。</li> <li>选择查看令牌用量活动，或兑换可用的已获得额度重置。</li> <li>若要直接查看令牌用量活动，请输入 <code>/usage daily</code>、<code>/usage weekly</code> 或 <code>/usage cumulative</code>。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会打开用量操作，或显示所选视图对应的 账户令牌活动。如果此会话没有 Codex 服务账户身份验证，Codex 会提示你登录。</p> <p><a id=\"inspect-config-layers-with-debug-config\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"debug-config\">使用 <code>/debug-config</code> 检查配置层</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/debug-config</code>。</li> <li>查看输出中的配置层级顺序（从最低优先级开始）、启用/停用 状态以及策略来源。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会显示配置层级诊断以及策略详情，例如 <code>allowed_approval_policies</code>, <code>allowed_sandbox_modes</code>, <code>mcp_servers</code>, <code>rules</code>, 以及已配置的 <code>experimental_network</code>。</p> <p>使用此输出排查生效设置与 <code>config.toml</code> 中的值不一致的原因。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-footer-items-with-statusline\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"statusline\">使用 <code>/statusline</code> 配置状态栏项目</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/statusline</code>。</li> <li>使用选择器切换项目并调整其顺序，然后确认。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：页脚状态行会立即更新，并将设置保存到 <code>config.toml</code> 中的 <code>tui.status_line</code>。</p> <p>可显示的状态行项目包括模型、模型与推理强度、上下文统计、速率 限制、Git 分支、令牌计数器、会话 ID、当前目录/项目根目录， 以及 Codex 版本。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-terminal-title-items-with-title\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"title\">使用 <code>/title</code> 配置终端标题项目</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/title</code>。</li> <li>使用选择器切换项目并调整其顺序，然后确认。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：终端窗口或标签页标题会立即更新，并将设置保存到 <code>config.toml</code> 中的 <code>tui.terminal_title</code>。</p> <p>可显示的标题项目包括应用名称、项目、活动指示器、状态、线程、Git 分支、模型和任务进度。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-syntax-theme-with-theme\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"theme\">使用 <code>/theme</code> 选择语法主题</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/theme</code>。</li> <li>在选择器中预览主题，然后确认。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会更新语法高亮，并将此选择保存到 <code>config.toml</code> 中的 <code>tui.theme</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-terminal-pet-with-pets\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"pets\">使用 <code>/pets</code> 选择终端宠物</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/pets</code>（或 <code>/pet</code>）打开宠物选择器。</li> <li>选择内置或自定义宠物，也可以关闭宠物功能。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会在支持的终端中显示所选的伴随宠物，并 保存该选择。也可以输入 <code>/pets off</code> 将其隐藏。</p> <p><a id=\"remap-tui-shortcuts-with-keymap\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"keymap-tui\">使用 <code>/keymap</code> 重新映射 TUI 快捷键</h3> <p>使用 <code>/keymap</code> 查看、更新并保存 TUI 的键盘快捷键绑定。</p> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/keymap</code>。</li> <li>选择要修改的快捷键上下文和操作。</li> <li>输入新的按键绑定，或移除现有绑定。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会更新当前键位映射，并将自定义按键绑定写入 <code>config.toml</code> 中的 <code>tui.keymap</code>。</p> <p>按键绑定使用 <code>ctrl-a</code>、<code>shift-enter</code> 和 <code>page-down</code> 等名称。上下文专属绑定会覆盖 <code>tui.keymap.global</code>；空绑定列表会取消该操作的绑定。</p> <p><a id=\"check-background-terminals-with-ps\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"ps\">使用 <code>/ps</code> 查看后台终端</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/ps</code>。</li> <li>检查后台终端列表及其状态。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会显示每个后台终端运行的命令，以及最多三行 最近的非空输出，让你快速了解进展。</p> <p>使用 <code>unified_exec</code> 时会显示后台终端；否则，列表可能为空。</p> <p><a id=\"stop-background-terminals-with-stop\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"stop\">使用 <code>/stop</code> 停止后台终端</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/stop</code>。</li> <li>如果 Codex 在停止所列终端前征求确认，请确认操作。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会停止当前会话的所有后台终端。<code>/clean</code> 仍可作为 <code>/stop</code> 的别名使用。</p> <p><a id=\"keep-transcripts-lean-with-compact\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"compact\">使用 <code>/compact</code> 精简聊天记录</h3> <ol> <li>长时间交流后，输入 <code>/compact</code>。</li> <li>Codex 提议总结当前聊天内容时，确认是否继续。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会用简明摘要替换较早的轮次，释放上下文空间， 同时保留关键信息。</p> <p><a id=\"review-changes-with-diff\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"diff\">使用 <code>/diff</code> 审查更改</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/diff</code> 查看 Git 差异。</li> <li>在 CLI 输出中滚动查看修改内容和新增文件。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会显示已暂存的更改、尚未暂存的更改， 以及 Git 尚未开始跟踪的文件，供你决定保留哪些内容。</p> <p><a id=\"highlight-files-with-mention\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"mention\">使用 <code>/mention</code> 标记文件</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/mention</code>，后接路径，例如 <code>/mention src/lib/api.ts</code>。</li> <li>从弹出窗口中选择匹配结果。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会将该文件添加到聊天中，使后续轮次能够直接引用它。</p> <p><a id=\"start-a-new-conversation-with-new\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"start-a-new-chat-with-new\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"new\">使用 <code>/new</code> 开始新聊天</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/new</code>，然后按 Enter。</li> <li>如果 Codex 提供检出方式选项，选择当前目录或新的工作树。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会在同一 CLI 会话中开始新的聊天，这样你 无需离开终端就能切换聊天。</p> <p>若要在创建新聊天时为其命名，请运行 <code>/new bug bash</code>。</p> <p>与 <code>/clear</code> 不同，<code>/new</code> 不会先清空当前终端视图。</p> <p><a id=\"rename-the-current-chat-with-rename\"></a> <a id=\"rename-the-current-task-with-rename\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"rename\">使用 <code>/rename</code> 重命名当前聊天</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/rename &lt;name&gt;</code>；也可以只输入 <code>/rename</code> 打开重命名提示框。</li> <li>输入一个简短名称，方便日后找到这段聊天。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会更新已保存的聊天名称，但不会更改聊天记录。</p> <p><a id=\"resume-a-saved-conversation-with-resume\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"resume-a-saved-chat-with-resume\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"resume\">使用 <code>/resume</code> 恢复已保存的聊天</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/resume</code>，然后按 Enter。</li> <li>在已保存会话选择器中选取所需会话。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会重新加载所选聊天的记录，让你可以从 上次中断处继续，同时保留原有历史记录。</p> <p><a id=\"fork-the-current-conversation-with-fork\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"fork-the-current-chat-with-fork\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"fork\">使用 <code>/fork</code> 分叉当前聊天</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/fork</code>，然后按 Enter。</li> <li>如果 Codex 提供检出方式选项，选择当前目录或新的工作树。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会将当前聊天克隆为一段新聊天，并为其分配新的 ID，同时保留原聊天记录不变，让你可以并行尝试其他 方案。</p> <p>如果要分叉已保存的会话，而不是当前会话，请运行 在终端中运行 <code>codex fork</code> 可打开会话选择器。</p> <p><a id=\"continue-in-the-desktop-app-with-app\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"app\">使用 <code>/app</code> 在桌面应用中继续</h3> <p>在 macOS 和 Windows 上，输入 <code>/app</code> 可在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中打开当前会话。如果应用尚未安装或正在运行，Codex 会显示错误并提示你 安装或启动应用。</p> <p>预期结果：桌面应用会打开同一段已保存的聊天，供你继续交流。</p> <p><a id=\"start-a-side-conversation-with-side\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"start-a-side-chat-with-side\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"side\">使用 <code>/side</code> 开始侧边聊天</h3> <p>使用 <code>/side</code> 从当前聊天创建临时分支，而不会离开主聊天。</p> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/side</code> 打开侧边聊天。</li> <li>也可以添加内嵌文本，例如 <code>/side Check whether this plan has an obvious risk</code>。</li> <li>专注处理的临时分支结束后，返回父聊天。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会打开侧边聊天，其聊天记录与 父聊天分开。在侧边聊天模式下，TUI 仍会显示 父聊天的状态，让你了解主聊天是否仍在运行。</p> <p>在另一个侧边聊天内或审查模式下，无法使用 <code>/side</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"generate-agentsmd-with-init\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"init-agentsmd\">使用 <code>/init</code> 生成 <code>AGENTS.md</code></h3> <ol> <li>在你希望 Codex 查找持久化指令的目录中运行 <code>/init</code>。</li> <li>检查生成的 <code>AGENTS.md</code>，再根据你的代码库约定进行编辑。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会创建 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 初始模板，你可以完善后提交，以供 之后的会话使用。</p> <p><a id=\"ask-for-a-working-tree-review-with-review\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"review\">使用 <code>/review</code> 请求审查工作树</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/review</code>。</li> <li>如果要查看具体文件改动，可再运行 <code>/diff</code>。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会总结在工作树中发现的问题，重点关注 行为变化和缺失的测试。除非你在 <code>config.toml</code> 中设置 <code>review_model</code>，否则它会使用当前会话的模型。</p> <p><a id=\"list-mcp-tools-with-mcp\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"mcp-mcp\">使用 <code>/mcp</code> 列出 MCP 工具</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/mcp</code>。</li> <li>查看列表，确认当前可用的 MCP 服务器和工具。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：你会看到本会话中已配置、可供 Codex 调用的模型上下文协议（MCP）工具。</p> <p>使用 <code>/mcp verbose</code> 查看详细的服务器诊断信息。使用 <code>/mcp login &lt;name&gt;</code> 可在当前会话中登录已配置的 MCP 服务器。</p> <p><a id=\"browse-apps-with-apps\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"apps\">使用 <code>/apps</code> 浏览应用</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/apps</code>。</li> <li>从列表中选择一个应用。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会在输入框中插入应用提及标记 <code>$app-slug</code>，这样 你就可以立即要求 Codex 使用该应用。</p> <p><a id=\"browse-plugins-with-plugins\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"plugins\">使用 <code>/plugins</code> 浏览插件</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/plugins</code>。</li> <li>选择一个市场选项卡，再选择插件以查看其功能或可用操作。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会打开插件浏览器，供你查看已安装的插件、 配置允许发现的插件，以及已安装插件的状态。 选中已安装的插件后按 <kbd>Space</kbd>，即可切换其启用状态。</p> <p><a id=\"view-and-manage-lifecycle-hooks-with-hooks\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"hooks\">使用 <code>/hooks</code> 查看和管理生命周期钩子</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/hooks</code>。</li> <li>选择一个钩子事件，查看与之对应的处理程序。</li> <li>根据需要信任、停用或重新启用非托管钩子。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会打开钩子浏览器，供你查看已配置的生命周期 钩子。受管理的钩子会标记为“受管理”，无法在用户钩子 浏览器中停用。</p> <p><a id=\"manage-chats-with-agents\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"agents\">使用 <code>/agents</code> 管理聊天</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/agents</code>，然后按 Enter。</li> <li>在命令中心选择一段聊天并打开。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会显示已连接服务器上的聊天概览。你可以查看聊天状态并在聊天之间切换。若要直接从终端打开命令中心，请运行 <code>codex agents</code>。命令中心需要连接到共享的本地或远程服务器。</p> <p><a id=\"switch-agent-threads-with-agent\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"switch-agent-threads-with-subagents\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"subagents\">使用 <code>/subagents</code> 切换智能体线程</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/subagents</code>，然后按 Enter。</li> <li>在选择器中选取所需线程。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会切换到该活动线程，供你查看或继续处理 该智能体的工作。</p> <p><a id=\"send-feedback-with-feedback\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"feedback\">使用 <code>/feedback</code> 发送反馈</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/feedback</code>，然后按 Enter。</li> <li>按照提示附上日志或诊断信息。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会收集所需的诊断信息，并提交给 维护人员。</p> <p><a id=\"sign-out-with-logout\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"logout\">使用 <code>/logout</code> 退出登录</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/logout</code>，然后按 Enter。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会清除当前用户会话的本地凭据。</p> <p><a id=\"exit-the-cli-with-quit-or-exit\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"quit-exit-cli\">使用 <code>/quit</code> 或 <code>/exit</code> 退出 CLI</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/quit</code>（或 <code>/exit</code>），然后按 Enter。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会立即退出。请先保存或提交重要工作。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>使用这些命令可通过 VS Code 命令面板控制 Codex。你也可以为它们绑定键盘快捷键。</p> <p><a id=\"assign-a-key-binding\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">分配快捷键</h2> <p>要为 Codex 命令设置或更改按键绑定，请按以下步骤操作：</p> <ol> <li>打开命令面板（macOS 按 <strong>Cmd+Shift+P</strong>；Windows/Linux 按 <strong>Ctrl+Shift+P</strong>）。</li> <li>运行 <strong>Preferences: Open Keyboard Shortcuts（首选项：打开键盘快捷方式）</strong>。</li> <li>搜索 <code>Codex</code> 或命令 ID（例如 <code>chatgpt.newChat</code>）。</li> <li>选择铅笔图标，然后输入所需快捷键。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"extension-commands\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_12\">扩展命令</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>命令</th> <th>默认键盘快捷键</th> <th>说明</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.addToThread</code></td> <td>-</td> <td>将选中的文本范围作为当前聊天的上下文添加</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.addFileToThread</code></td> <td>-</td> <td>将整个文件作为当前聊天的上下文添加</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.newChat</code></td> <td>macOS：<code>Cmd+N</code><br>Windows/Linux：<code>Ctrl+N</code></td> <td>创建新聊天</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.newCodexPanel</code></td> <td>-</td> <td>创建新的 Codex 面板</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.openCommandMenu</code></td> <td>-</td> <td>打开 Codex 命令菜单</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.openSidebar</code></td> <td>-</td> <td>打开 Codex 侧边栏面板</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>使用斜杠命令，无需离开输入框即可控制 Codex。你可以用它们查看状态、切换本地与云端模式，或发送反馈。</p> <p><a id=\"use-a-slash-command\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_13\">使用斜杠命令</h2> <ol> <li>在 Codex 输入框中输入 <code>/</code>。</li> <li>从列表中选择命令，或继续输入以筛选（例如 <code>/status</code>）。</li> <li>按 <strong>Enter</strong>。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"available-slash-commands\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_14\">可用的斜杠命令</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>斜杠命令</th> <th>说明</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>/approve</code></td> <td>自动审查启用时，批准对最近一次被拒绝的操作重试一次。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/cloud</code></td> <td>在支持云端执行时，于云端运行聊天。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/cloud-environment</code></td> <td>为聊天选择云端环境。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/compact</code></td> <td>压缩当前聊天的上下文。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/fast</code></td> <td>在可用时，开启或关闭模型目录提供的 Fast 服务档位。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/feedback</code></td> <td>打开反馈对话框以提交反馈，也可以附上日志。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/fork</code></td> <td>将本地聊天复制为新的本地聊天。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/goal</code></td> <td>为 Codex 设置一个持续推进的目标。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/ide-context</code></td> <td>开启或关闭 IDE 上下文自动注入。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/init</code></td> <td>为当前项目生成 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 初始模板。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/local</code></td> <td>在本地工作区中运行聊天。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/mcp</code></td> <td>打开 MCP 状态，查看已连接的服务器。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/memories</code></td> <td>在记忆功能可用时，配置聊天是否可以使用或生成记忆。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/model</code></td> <td>为当前聊天选择模型。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/personality</code></td> <td>在当前模型支持交流风格时，选择 Codex 的回复方式。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/plan</code></td> <td>切换多步骤规划的计划模式。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/project</code></td> <td>为新聊天选择项目。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/reasoning</code></td> <td>为当前聊天选择推理强度。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/review</code></td> <td>启动代码审查模式，以审查未提交的更改或与基准分支进行比较。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/side</code></td> <td>在不中断主聊天的情况下，开始临时侧边聊天。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/status</code></td> <td>显示聊天 ID、上下文用量和速率限制。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/worktree</code></td> <td>在新的 Git worktree 中运行聊天。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table>","en":"<h1 id=\"developer-commands\">Developer commands</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT web has its own composer command menu. Type <code>/</code> to see the actions available in the current chat. It doesn't expose the ChatGPT desktop app or CLI command set; the Codex slash commands, CLI commands, and flags in this reference don't apply to ChatGPT web.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"chatgpt-desktop-app-commands\">ChatGPT desktop app commands</h2> <p>The general <a href=\"#/article/a-dd7bb821828a3c32\">Commands</a> page covers app navigation, chat shortcuts, keyboard customization, and deep links for chats, settings, skills, scheduled tasks, plugins, and pets.</p> <p>The <a href=\"#/article/a-6c3aed9dab628df5\">Slash commands</a> page covers the commands available from the app composer, including <code>/feedback</code>, <code>/goal</code>, <code>/init</code>, <code>/mcp</code>, <code>/plan</code>, <code>/review</code>, and <code>/status</code>.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"how-to-read-this-reference\">How to read this reference</h2> <p>This page catalogs every documented Codex CLI command and flag. Use the interactive tables to search by key or description. Each section shows the option's maturity and flags deprecated options and risky combinations.</p> <p>The CLI inherits most defaults from <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>. Any <code>-c key=value</code> overrides you pass at the command line take precedence for that invocation. See <a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76?anchor=configuration-precedence\">Config basics</a> for more information.</p> <h2 id=\"global-flags\">Global flags</h2> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>globalFlagOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>These options apply to the base <code>codex</code> command. Most propagate to commands; see the notes above or the relevant command help for exceptions. For propagated flags, follow the relevant command help. For example, <code>codex exec --oss ...</code> applies <code>--oss</code> to <code>exec</code>.</p> <h2 id=\"command-overview\">Command overview</h2> <p>The Maturity column uses feature maturity labels such as Experimental, Beta, Stable, and Deprecated. See <a href=\"#/article/a-d303113c34a6b1a9\">Feature Maturity</a> for how to interpret these labels.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>commandOverview</code></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"command-details\">Command details</h2> <h3 id=\"codex-interactive\"><code>codex</code> (interactive)</h3> <p>Running <code>codex</code> with no subcommand launches the interactive terminal UI (TUI). The agent accepts the global flags above plus image attachments. Web search defaults to cached mode; use <code>--search</code> to switch to live browsing. For low-friction local work, use <code>--sandbox workspace-write --ask-for-approval on-request</code>.</p> <p>Use <code>--remote ws://host:port</code> or <code>--remote wss://host:port</code> to connect the TUI to an app server started with <code>codex app-server --listen ws://IP:PORT</code>. For a local Unix socket, use <code>--remote unix://</code> for the default socket or <code>--remote unix://PATH</code> for an explicit path. Add <code>--remote-auth-token-env &lt;ENV_VAR&gt;</code> when the server requires a bearer token for WebSocket authentication.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-agents\"><code>codex agents</code></h3> <p>Open the command center to browse chats and switch between agents on a shared server. Use <code>--remote &lt;URL&gt;</code> to connect to a remote server and <code>--cd &lt;DIR&gt;</code> to set the directory for new remote tasks. <code>codex agents</code> doesn't support <code>--no-daemon</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-queue\"><code>codex queue</code></h3> <p>Queue a text message for an existing session:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex queue --thread &lt;SESSION_ID&gt; --message \"Run the remaining checks\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>--thread</code> accepts a UUID or exact session name. Use a UUID when sessions share the same name. The command also accepts <code>--remote</code> and <code>--remote-auth-token-env</code>; image attachments aren't supported.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-app-server\"><code>codex app-server</code></h3> <p>Launch the Codex app server locally. This is primarily for development and debugging and may change without notice.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>appServerOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>codex app-server --listen stdio://</code> keeps the default JSONL-over-stdio behavior, and <code>codex app-server --stdio</code> is an alias for that transport. <code>--listen ws://IP:PORT</code> enables WebSocket transport for app-server clients. The server accepts <code>ws://</code> listen URLs; use TLS termination or a secure proxy when clients connect with <code>wss://</code>. Use <code>--listen unix://</code> to accept WebSocket handshakes on Codex's default Unix socket, or <code>--listen unix:///absolute/path.sock</code> to choose a socket path. If you generate schemas for client bindings, add <code>--experimental</code> to include gated fields and methods.</p> <p>Add <code>--code-mode-host wss://code-mode.example.com/host</code> to connect app-server to a remote Code Mode host instead of starting a local host. This outbound connection is separate from <code>--listen</code> and shared by every thread in the app-server process. Use <code>ws://</code> only for a localhost or SSH-forwarded host.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-remote-control\"><code>codex remote-control</code></h3> <p>Run <code>codex remote-control</code> to start remote control through the managed background server when eligible, with a foreground fallback. Use <code>codex remote-control --no-daemon</code> to run in the foreground explicitly. Use <code>codex remote-control start</code> to start the local app-server daemon with remote control enabled, and <code>codex remote-control stop</code> to stop it. Managed remote-control clients and SSH remote workflows use these commands; they aren't a replacement for <code>codex app-server --listen</code> when you're building a local protocol client.</p> <p>After the daemon is running, use <code>codex remote-control pair</code> to create and print a short-lived manual pairing code. Add <code>--json</code> to any remote-control command for machine-readable output. For <code>pair</code>, the JSON response includes <code>pairingCode</code>, <code>manualPairingCode</code>, <code>environmentId</code>, and <code>expiresAt</code>. <code>--no-daemon</code> applies only to the bare <code>remote-control</code> command; don't combine it with <code>start</code>, <code>stop</code>, or <code>pair</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-app\"><code>codex app</code></h3> <p>Launch the ChatGPT desktop app from the terminal on macOS or Windows. On macOS, Codex can open a specific workspace path; on Windows, Codex prints the path to open.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>appOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>codex app</code> opens an installed ChatGPT desktop app, or starts the installer when the app is missing. On macOS, Codex opens the provided workspace path; on Windows, it prints the path to open after installation.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-debug-app-server-send-message-v2\"><code>codex debug app-server send-message-v2</code></h3> <p>Send one message through app-server's V2 thread/turn flow using the built-in app-server test client.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>debugAppServerSendMessageV2Options</code></p> </blockquote> <p>This debug flow initializes with <code>experimentalApi: true</code>, starts a thread, sends a turn, and streams server notifications. Use it to reproduce and inspect app-server protocol behavior locally.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-debug-models\"><code>codex debug models</code></h3> <p>Print the raw model catalog Codex sees as JSON.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>debugModelsOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>Use <code>--bundled</code> when you want to inspect only the catalog bundled with the current binary, without refreshing from the remote models endpoint.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-debug-prompt-input\"><code>codex debug prompt-input</code></h3> <p>Render the exact model-visible prompt input list as JSON. Use this when debugging instruction discovery, session context, or prompt construction.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>debugPromptInputOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-apply\"><code>codex apply</code></h3> <p>Apply the most recent diff from a Codex cloud chat to your local repository. You must authenticate and have access to the chat.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>applyOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>Codex prints the patched files and exits non-zero if <code>git apply</code> fails (for example, due to conflicts).</p> <h3 id=\"codex-review\"><code>codex review</code></h3> <p>Run a code review non-interactively. Choose exactly one review target, or pass custom review instructions as a prompt.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>reviewOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>--uncommitted</code>, <code>--base</code>, <code>--commit</code>, and a custom <code>PROMPT</code> conflict with one another. Use <code>--title</code> only with <code>--commit</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-archive-and-codex-unarchive\"><code>codex archive</code> and <code>codex unarchive</code></h3> <p>Archive or restore a saved interactive session by session ID or session name. Use these commands when you want to clean up the session picker without deleting the transcript. Session IDs take precedence over session names.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex archive &lt;SESSION&gt;\ncodex unarchive &lt;SESSION&gt;\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>archiveOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-delete\"><code>codex delete</code></h3> <p>Permanently delete a saved interactive session by session ID or session name. Use this only when you want to remove the transcript instead of hiding it from active session lists.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex delete &lt;SESSION&gt;\ncodex delete &lt;SESSION_UUID&gt; --force\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>deleteOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>Use <code>--force</code> only with a session UUID. Named sessions still require confirmation so Codex doesn't delete a repeated or ambiguous name without a prompt.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-cloud\"><code>codex cloud</code></h3> <p>Interact with Codex cloud chats from the terminal. The default command opens an interactive picker; <code>codex cloud exec</code> submits a task directly, and <code>codex cloud list</code> returns recent chats for scripting or quick inspection.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>cloudExecOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>Authentication follows the same credentials as the main CLI. Codex exits non-zero if the task submission fails.</p> <h4 id=\"codex-cloud-list\"><code>codex cloud list</code></h4> <p>List recent cloud chats with optional filtering and pagination.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>cloudListOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>Plain-text output prints a task URL followed by status details. Use <code>--json</code> for automation. The JSON payload contains a <code>tasks</code> array plus an optional <code>cursor</code> value. Each task includes <code>id</code>, <code>url</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>status</code>, <code>updated_at</code>, <code>environment_id</code>, <code>environment_label</code>, <code>summary</code>, <code>is_review</code>, and <code>attempt_total</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-completion\"><code>codex completion</code></h3> <p>Generate shell completion scripts and redirect the output to the appropriate location, for example <code>codex completion zsh &gt; \"${fpath[1]}/_codex\"</code>.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>completionOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-doctor\"><code>codex doctor</code></h3> <p>Generate a local diagnostic report before filing a support issue or while investigating a broken Codex installation. The report checks installation, configuration, authentication, runtime, Git, terminal, app-server, and thread inventory health.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>doctorOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-features\"><code>codex features</code></h3> <p>Manage feature flags stored in <code>$CODEX_HOME/config.toml</code>. The <code>enable</code> and <code>disable</code> commands persist changes so they apply to future sessions. The <code>features</code> subcommand doesn't accept <code>--profile</code>.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>featuresOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-exec\"><code>codex exec</code></h3> <p>Use <code>codex exec</code> (or the short form <code>codex e</code>) for scripted or CI-style runs that should finish without human interaction.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>execOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>Codex writes formatted output by default. Add <code>--json</code> to receive newline-delimited JSON events (one per state change). The optional <code>resume</code> subcommand lets you continue non-interactive tasks. Use <code>--last</code> to pick the most recent session from the current working directory, or add <code>--all</code> to search across all sessions:</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>execResumeOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>Use <code>codex exec fork &lt;SESSION_ID&gt; [PROMPT]</code> to copy a saved session into a new session. The session argument accepts a UUID or name. With no prompt, Codex creates the fork without starting a turn. Pass <code>-</code> as the prompt to read it from stdin, or add <code>--image</code> to attach images.</p> <p>A prompt is required when using images, <code>--output-schema</code>, <code>--output-last-message</code>, or <code>--ephemeral</code>.</p> <p>Add <code>--worktree</code> to a new or forked run to create a managed Git worktree:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex exec --worktree \"implement the next step\"\ncodex exec fork &lt;SESSION_ID&gt; --worktree \"try an alternative approach\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>--worktree</code> requires local execution. Don't combine it with <code>resume</code>, <code>review</code>, <code>--ephemeral</code>, or <code>--ignore-user-config</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-execpolicy\"><code>codex execpolicy</code></h3> <p>Check <code>execpolicy</code> rule files before you save them. <code>codex execpolicy check</code> accepts one or more <code>--rules</code> flags (for example, files under <code>~/.codex/rules</code>) and emits JSON showing the strictest decision and any matching rules. Add <code>--pretty</code> to format the output. The <code>execpolicy</code> command is currently in preview.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>execpolicyOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-login\"><code>codex login</code></h3> <p>Authenticate the CLI with a ChatGPT account, API key, or access token. With no flags, Codex opens a browser for the ChatGPT OAuth flow.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>loginOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>codex login status</code> exits with <code>0</code> when credentials are present, which is helpful in automation scripts.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-logout\"><code>codex logout</code></h3> <p>Remove saved credentials for both API key and ChatGPT authentication. This command has no flags.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-mcp\"><code>codex mcp</code></h3> <p>Manage Model Context Protocol server entries stored in <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>mcpCommands</code></p> </blockquote> <p>The <code>add</code> subcommand supports both stdio and streamable HTTP transports:</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>mcpAddOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>OAuth actions (<code>login</code>, <code>logout</code>) only work with streamable HTTP servers (and only when the server supports OAuth).</p> <h3 id=\"codex-plugin\"><code>codex plugin</code></h3> <p>Install, list, and remove plugins from configured marketplaces.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>pluginCommands</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>codex plugin add --json</code> prints <code>pluginId</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>marketplaceName</code>, <code>version</code>, <code>installedPath</code>, and <code>authPolicy</code>. <code>codex plugin list --json</code> prints <code>installed</code> and <code>available</code> arrays. Entries include <code>pluginId</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>marketplaceName</code>, <code>version</code>, <code>installed</code>, <code>enabled</code>, <code>source</code>, <code>installPolicy</code>, <code>authPolicy</code>, and, when available, <code>marketplaceSource</code> with the configured marketplace source type and value. <code>codex plugin remove --json</code> prints <code>pluginId</code>, <code>name</code>, and <code>marketplaceName</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-plugin-marketplace\"><code>codex plugin marketplace</code></h3> <p>Manage plugin marketplace sources that Codex can browse and install from.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>marketplaceCommands</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>codex plugin marketplace add</code> accepts GitHub shorthand such as <code>owner/repo</code> or <code>owner/repo@ref</code>, HTTP or HTTPS Git URLs, SSH Git URLs, and local marketplace root directories. Use <code>--ref</code> to pin a Git ref, and repeat <code>--sparse PATH</code> to use a sparse checkout for Git-backed marketplace repositories.</p> <p><code>codex plugin marketplace list</code> prints in-scope marketplace names and roots, including implicitly discovered default marketplaces and configured marketplace snapshots.</p> <p>Add <code>--json</code> to marketplace add, list, upgrade, or remove commands for automation-friendly output. Marketplace add JSON includes <code>marketplaceName</code>, <code>installedRoot</code>, and <code>alreadyAdded</code>; list JSON includes a <code>marketplaces</code> array with <code>name</code>, <code>root</code>, and optional <code>marketplaceSource</code>; upgrade JSON includes <code>selectedMarketplaces</code>, <code>upgradedRoots</code>, and <code>errors</code>; remove JSON includes <code>marketplaceName</code> and <code>installedRoot</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-mcp-server\"><code>codex mcp-server</code></h3> <p>The <code>codex mcp-server</code> command and standalone <code>codex-mcp-server</code> binary have been removed. Use the <a href=\"#/article/a-341246db376ea9e1\">Codex app server</a> instead.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-resume\"><code>codex resume</code></h3> <p>Continue an interactive session by ID or resume the most recent chat. <code>codex resume</code> scopes <code>--last</code> to the current working directory unless you pass <code>--all</code>. It accepts model and sandbox overrides, but not <code>--worktree</code>.</p> <p>If the current working directory differs from the session's saved directory, Codex asks which directory to use. Set <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\"><code>tui.resume_cwd</code></a> to <code>\"current\"</code> or <code>\"session\"</code> to reuse that choice without a prompt. An explicit <code>--cd</code> (<code>-C</code>) override takes precedence over <code>tui.resume_cwd</code>.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>resumeOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-fork\"><code>codex fork</code></h3> <p>Fork a previous interactive session into a new chat. By default, <code>codex fork</code> opens the session picker; add <code>--last</code> to fork your most recent session instead.</p> <p>When the current and saved session directories differ, <code>codex fork</code> uses the same working-directory prompt and <code>tui.resume_cwd</code> setting as <code>codex resume</code>.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>forkOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>To fork into a managed Git worktree, run <code>codex fork &lt;SESSION_ID&gt; --worktree</code>. This requires an explicit session ID and local execution; it doesn't support <code>--last</code> or the session picker.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-sandbox\"><code>codex sandbox</code></h3> <p>Use the sandbox helper to run a command under the same policies Codex uses internally.</p> <h4 id=\"macos-seatbelt\">macOS seatbelt</h4> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>sandboxMacOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"linux-landlock\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"linux-sandbox\">Linux sandbox</h4> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>sandboxLinuxOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h4 id=\"windows\">Windows</h4> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>sandboxWindowsOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-update\"><code>codex update</code></h3> <p>Check for and apply a Codex CLI update when the installed release supports self-update. Debug builds print a message telling you to install a release build instead.</p> <h2 id=\"flag-combinations-and-safety-tips\">Flag combinations and safety tips</h2> <ul> <li>Use <code>--sandbox workspace-write</code> for unattended local work that can stay inside the workspace, and avoid <code>--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox</code> unless you are inside a dedicated sandbox VM.</li> <li>When you need to grant Codex write access to more directories, prefer <code>--add-dir</code> rather than forcing <code>--sandbox danger-full-access</code>.</li> <li>Pair <code>--json</code> with <code>--output-last-message</code> in CI to capture machine-readable progress and a final natural-language summary.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"interactive-shortcuts\">Interactive shortcuts</h2> <ul> <li>Type <code>@</code> to search for a file in the workspace and add its path to the prompt.</li> <li>Press <kbd>Up</kbd> or <kbd>Down</kbd> to restore draft history.</li> <li>Press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>R</kbd> to search prompt history, then press <kbd>Enter</kbd> to use a match or <kbd>Escape</kbd> to cancel.</li> <li>Press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>O</kbd> or run <code>/copy</code> to copy the latest completed Codex output.</li> <li>Prefix a line with <code>!</code> to run a local shell command under the current approval and sandbox settings.</li> <li>Press <kbd>Tab</kbd> while Codex is working to queue a follow-up prompt, slash command, or shell command for the next turn.</li> <li>Press <kbd>Enter</kbd> while Codex is working to inject new instructions into the current turn.</li> <li>Press <kbd>Escape</kbd> twice with an empty composer to edit the previous user message and fork the chat from that point.</li> <li>Press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>C</kbd> or run <code>/exit</code> to close the session.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"related-resources\">Related resources</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d\">Codex CLI overview</a>: installation, upgrades, and quick tips.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">Config basics</a>: persist defaults like the model and provider.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85\">Advanced Config</a>: profiles, providers, sandbox tuning, and integrations.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-94f17e3de1ca7cb3\">AGENTS.md</a>: conceptual overview of Codex agent capabilities and best practices.</li> </ul> <p>Slash commands give you fast, keyboard-first control over Codex. Type <code>/</code> in the composer to open the slash popup, choose a command, and Codex will perform actions such as switching models, adjusting permissions, or summarizing long chats without leaving the terminal.</p> <p>This guide shows you how to:</p> <ul> <li>Find the right built-in slash command for a task</li> <li>Steer an active session with commands like <code>/model</code>, <code>/fast</code>, <code>/permissions</code>, <code>/approve</code>, <code>/raw</code>, <code>/agents</code>, <code>/subagents</code>, and <code>/status</code></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"built-in-slash-commands\">Built-in slash commands</h2> <p>Codex ships with the following commands. Open the slash popup and start typing the command name to filter the list.</p> <p>When a chat is already running, you can type a slash command and press <code>Tab</code> to queue it for the next turn. Codex parses queued slash commands when they run, so command menus and errors appear after the current turn finishes. Slash completion still works before you queue the command.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Command</th> <th>Purpose</th> <th>When to use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=update-permissions-with-permissions\"><code>/permissions</code></a></td> <td>Set what Codex can do without asking first.</td> <td>Relax or tighten approval requirements mid-session, such as switching between Auto and Read Only.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=include-ide-context-with-ide\"><code>/ide</code></a></td> <td>Include open files, current selection, and other IDE context.</td> <td>Pull editor context into the next prompt without re-explaining what's open in your IDE.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=remap-tui-shortcuts-with-keymap\"><code>/keymap</code></a></td> <td>Remap TUI keyboard shortcuts.</td> <td>Inspect and persist custom shortcut bindings in <code>config.toml</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=toggle-vim-mode-with-vim\"><code>/vim</code></a></td> <td>Toggle Vim mode for the composer.</td> <td>Switch between Vim normal/insert behavior and the default composer editing mode.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=set-up-the-elevated-windows-sandbox-with-setup-default-sandbox\"><code>/setup-default-sandbox</code></a></td> <td>Set up the elevated agent sandbox (Windows only).</td> <td>Replace the degraded Windows sandbox after Codex offers the elevated setup.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=manage-chats-with-agents\"><code>/agents</code></a></td> <td>Open the agent command center.</td> <td>Browse chats and switch between agents on the connected server.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=switch-agent-threads-with-subagents\"><code>/subagents</code></a></td> <td>Switch the active subagent thread.</td> <td>Inspect or continue work in a subagent from the current session.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=browse-apps-with-apps\"><code>/apps</code></a></td> <td>Browse apps (connectors) and insert them into your prompt.</td> <td>Attach an app as <code>$app-slug</code> before asking Codex to use it.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=browse-plugins-with-plugins\"><code>/plugins</code></a></td> <td>Browse installed and discoverable plugins.</td> <td>Inspect plugin tools, install suggested plugins, or manage plugin availability.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=view-and-manage-lifecycle-hooks-with-hooks\"><code>/hooks</code></a></td> <td>View and manage lifecycle hooks.</td> <td>Inspect configured hooks, trust new or changed hooks, or disable non-managed hooks before they run.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=clear-the-terminal-and-start-a-new-chat-with-clear\"><code>/clear</code></a></td> <td>Clear the terminal and start a fresh chat.</td> <td>Reset the visible UI and chat context together when you want a fresh start.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=rename-the-current-chat-with-rename\"><code>/rename</code></a></td> <td>Rename the current chat.</td> <td>Give a saved session a recognizable name without leaving the TUI.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=archive-the-current-session-with-archive\"><code>/archive</code></a></td> <td>Archive the current session.</td> <td>Remove the current session from active session lists without deleting its transcript.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=delete-the-current-session-with-delete\"><code>/delete</code></a></td> <td>Permanently delete the current session.</td> <td>Remove the transcript and descendant sessions when archiving isn't enough.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=keep-transcripts-lean-with-compact\"><code>/compact</code></a></td> <td>Summarize the visible chat to free tokens.</td> <td>Use after long runs so Codex retains key points without blowing the context window.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=copy-the-latest-response-with-copy\"><code>/copy</code></a></td> <td>Copy the latest completed Codex output.</td> <td>Grab the latest finished response or plan text without manually selecting it. You can also press <code>Ctrl+O</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=review-changes-with-diff\"><code>/diff</code></a></td> <td>Show the Git diff, including files Git isn't tracking yet.</td> <td>Review Codex's edits before you commit or run tests.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=exit-the-cli-with-quit-or-exit\"><code>/exit</code></a></td> <td>Exit the CLI (same as <code>/quit</code>).</td> <td>Alternative spelling; both commands exit the session.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=toggle-experimental-features-with-experimental\"><code>/experimental</code></a></td> <td>Toggle experimental features.</td> <td>Enable options such as Network proxy or Prevent sleep while running.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=approve-an-auto-review-denial-with-approve\"><code>/approve</code></a></td> <td>Approve one retry of a recent auto review denial.</td> <td>Retry a command or action that the auto reviewer denied.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=configure-memories-with-memories\"><code>/memories</code></a></td> <td>Configure memory use and generation.</td> <td>Turn memory injection or memory generation on or off without leaving the TUI.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=use-skills-with-skills\"><code>/skills</code></a></td> <td>Browse and use skills.</td> <td>Improve task-specific behavior by selecting a relevant local skill.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=import-claude-code-or-cursor-setup-with-import\"><code>/import</code></a></td> <td>Import Claude Code or Cursor setup, projects, and chats.</td> <td>Migrate supported external-agent artifacts into Codex configuration and local files.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=send-feedback-with-feedback\"><code>/feedback</code></a></td> <td>Send logs to the Codex maintainers.</td> <td>Report issues or share diagnostics with support.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=generate-agentsmd-with-init\"><code>/init</code></a></td> <td>Generate an <code>AGENTS.md</code> scaffold in the current directory.</td> <td>Capture persistent instructions for the repository or subdirectory you're working in.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=sign-out-with-logout\"><code>/logout</code></a></td> <td>Sign out of Codex.</td> <td>Clear local credentials when using a shared machine.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=list-mcp-tools-with-mcp\"><code>/mcp</code></a></td> <td>List configured Model Context Protocol (MCP) tools.</td> <td>Check which external tools Codex can call during the session; add <code>verbose</code> for server details.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=highlight-files-with-mention\"><code>/mention</code></a></td> <td>Attach a file to the chat.</td> <td>Point Codex at specific files or folders you want it to inspect next.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=set-the-active-model-with-model\"><code>/model</code></a></td> <td>Choose the active model (and reasoning effort, when available).</td> <td>Use <code>gpt-6-luna</code> or <code>gpt-6.1-sol</code> if shown.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=toggle-fast-mode-with-fast\"><code>/fast</code></a></td> <td>Toggle a Fast service tier when the model catalog exposes one.</td> <td>Turn the current model's Fast tier on or off and persist the selection.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=switch-to-plan-mode-with-plan\"><code>/plan</code></a></td> <td>Switch to plan mode and optionally send a prompt.</td> <td>Ask Codex to propose an execution plan before implementation work starts.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=set-or-view-a-task-goal-with-goal\"><code>/goal</code></a></td> <td>Set, edit, pause, resume, view, or clear a task goal.</td> <td>Give Codex a persistent target to track while a larger task runs.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=check-background-terminals-with-ps\"><code>/ps</code></a></td> <td>Show background terminals and their recent output.</td> <td>Check long-running commands without leaving the main transcript.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=stop-background-terminals-with-stop\"><code>/stop</code></a></td> <td>Stop all background terminals.</td> <td>Cancel background terminal work started by the current session.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=fork-the-current-chat-with-fork\"><code>/fork</code></a></td> <td>Fork the current chat into a new chat.</td> <td>Branch the active session to explore a new approach without losing the current transcript.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=continue-in-the-desktop-app-with-app\"><code>/app</code></a></td> <td>Continue the current session in the ChatGPT desktop app.</td> <td>Move from the TUI to the desktop app on macOS or Windows.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=start-a-side-chat-with-side\"><code>/side</code>, <code>/btw</code></a></td> <td>Start an ephemeral side chat.</td> <td>Ask a focused follow-up without disrupting the main chat's transcript.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=toggle-raw-scrollback-with-raw\"><code>/raw</code></a></td> <td>Toggle raw scrollback mode.</td> <td>Make terminal selection and copying less formatted while reviewing long output.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=resume-a-saved-chat-with-resume\"><code>/resume</code></a></td> <td>Resume a saved chat from your session list.</td> <td>Continue work from a previous CLI session without starting over.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=start-a-new-chat-with-new\"><code>/new</code></a></td> <td>Start a new chat inside the same CLI session.</td> <td>Reset the chat context without leaving the CLI when you want a fresh prompt in the same repo.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=exit-the-cli-with-quit-or-exit\"><code>/quit</code></a></td> <td>Exit the CLI.</td> <td>Leave the session immediately.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=ask-for-a-working-tree-review-with-review\"><code>/review</code></a></td> <td>Ask Codex to review your working tree.</td> <td>Run after Codex completes work or when you want a second set of eyes on local changes.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=inspect-the-session-with-status\"><code>/status</code></a></td> <td>Display session configuration and token usage.</td> <td>Confirm the active model, approval policy, writable roots, and remaining context capacity.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=view-account-usage-with-usage\"><code>/usage</code></a></td> <td>View account token usage or use a rate-limit reset.</td> <td>Inspect daily, weekly, or cumulative ChatGPT token activity from inside the TUI.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=inspect-config-layers-with-debug-config\"><code>/debug-config</code></a></td> <td>Print config layer and requirements diagnostics.</td> <td>Debug precedence and policy requirements, including experimental network constraints.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=configure-footer-items-with-statusline\"><code>/statusline</code></a></td> <td>Configure TUI status-line fields interactively.</td> <td>Pick and reorder footer items (model/context/limits/git/tokens/session) and persist in config.toml.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=configure-terminal-title-items-with-title\"><code>/title</code></a></td> <td>Configure terminal window or tab title fields interactively.</td> <td>Pick and reorder title items such as project, status, thread, branch, model, and task progress.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=choose-a-syntax-theme-with-theme\"><code>/theme</code></a></td> <td>Choose a syntax-highlighting theme.</td> <td>Preview and persist a terminal syntax-highlighting theme.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=choose-a-terminal-pet-with-pets\"><code>/pets</code>, <code>/pet</code></a></td> <td>Choose or hide a terminal pet.</td> <td>Personalize the TUI with a built-in or custom ambient pet.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=choose-the-terminal-mode-with-tui\"><code>/tui</code></a></td> <td>Choose the terminal mode for the next launch.</td> <td>Switch between terminal scrollback and a fullscreen transcript.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=export-a-conversation-with-export\"><code>/export</code></a></td> <td>Export the conversation as Markdown.</td> <td>Save a complete transcript to a file or copy it to the clipboard.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=summarize-the-chat-with-recap\"><code>/recap</code></a></td> <td>Generate a summary of the current conversation.</td> <td>Catch up on the chat without compacting its context.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=change-directories-with-cd\"><code>/cd</code></a></td> <td>Change the session's working directory.</td> <td>Continue an idle primary chat in another directory.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=change-directories-with-cd\"><code>/pwd</code>, <code>/cwd</code></a></td> <td>Show the working directory.</td> <td>Check the directory the active session uses.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=continue-in-a-worktree-with-worktree\"><code>/worktree</code></a></td> <td>Start or continue a chat in a managed Git worktree.</td> <td>Work in a separate checkout of a local repository.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=manage-the-background-server-with-daemon\"><code>/daemon</code></a></td> <td>Open background server controls.</td> <td>Inspect the connection and manage a local server owned by Codex.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=inspect-warnings-with-warnings\"><code>/warnings</code></a></td> <td>View retained warnings and diagnostics.</td> <td>Revisit warnings that appeared during the session.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><code>/quit</code> and <code>/exit</code> both exit the CLI. Use them only after you have saved or committed any important work.</p> <p>Use <code>/permissions</code> to adjust what Codex can do without asking first. Use <code>/approve</code> only when you need to retry a recent action that automatic review denied.</p> <h2 id=\"control-your-session-with-slash-commands\">Control your session with slash commands</h2> <p>The following workflows keep your session on track without restarting Codex.</p> <h3 id=\"choose-the-terminal-mode-with-tui\">Choose the terminal mode with <code>/tui</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/tui</code>.</li> <li>Choose scrollback or fullscreen mode, then confirm.</li> <li>Restart Codex to apply the selection.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: The next launch uses the saved terminal mode. Launch overrides such as <code>--no-alt-screen</code> still apply.</p> <h3 id=\"export-a-conversation-with-export\">Export a conversation with <code>/export</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/export</code>.</li> <li>Choose <strong>Copy to clipboard</strong> or <strong>Save to file</strong>.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex exports the complete conversation as Markdown. To save directly to a file, run <code>/export session.md</code>. Wait for the current turn to finish before exporting.</p> <h3 id=\"summarize-the-chat-with-recap\">Summarize the chat with <code>/recap</code></h3> <ol> <li>When Codex is idle, type <code>/recap</code>.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex generates a summary of the conversation, even if <code>tui.auto_recap = false</code>. Use <code>/compact</code> when you want to free context space.</p> <h3 id=\"change-directories-with-cd\">Change directories with <code>/cd</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/pwd</code> (or <code>/cwd</code>) to check the current directory.</li> <li>Type <code>/cd &lt;path&gt;</code> to change directories, or <code>/cd</code> to use your home directory.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex continues the chat in the selected directory. Changing directories requires an idle primary session with no queued input or background terminals.</p> <h3 id=\"continue-in-a-worktree-with-worktree\">Continue in a worktree with <code>/worktree</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/worktree</code> in a local Git repository.</li> <li>Choose whether to start a new chat or continue the current conversation in a new worktree.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex creates a managed Git worktree and starts the selected chat there. Choose <strong>Browse worktrees</strong> to find existing worktrees and their owner chats. This command requires local worktree support and is unavailable while a task is running.</p> <h3 id=\"manage-the-background-server-with-daemon\">Manage the background server with <code>/daemon</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/daemon</code>.</li> <li>Review the server connection and available actions.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex offers to install the latest public stable release or use the current CLI build for the local background server. Confirming an update exits Codex and may interrupt active work. For a remote connection, manage the server on its host.</p> <h3 id=\"inspect-warnings-with-warnings\">Inspect warnings with <code>/warnings</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/warnings</code>.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex shows retained warnings and their diagnostic details.</p> <h3 id=\"set-the-active-model-with-model\">Set the active model with <code>/model</code></h3> <p>The picker only shows models available to your account and workspace. If GPT-6.1 Sol isn't listed, choose another model. See <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6.1-sol\">GPT-6.1 Sol availability by plan</a>.</p> <ol> <li>Start Codex and open the composer.</li> <li>Type <code>/model</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>Choose a model such as <code>gpt-6-luna</code> or <code>gpt-6.1-sol</code> from the popup.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex confirms the new model in the transcript. Run <code>/status</code> to verify the change.</p> <h3 id=\"toggle-fast-mode-with-fast\">Toggle Fast mode with <code>/fast</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/fast</code> to turn the current model's Fast service tier on.</li> <li>Type <code>/fast</code> again to turn it off.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex toggles the tier and saves the selection. In the TUI footer, you can also show a Fast mode status-line item with <code>/statusline</code>.</p> <p>Fast tier commands are catalog-driven. If the current model doesn't advertise a Fast tier, Codex won't show <code>/fast</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"switch-to-plan-mode-with-plan\">Switch to plan mode with <code>/plan</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/plan</code> and press Enter to switch the active chat into plan mode.</li> <li>Optional: provide inline prompt text (for example, <code>/plan Propose a\nmigration plan for this service</code>).</li> <li>You can paste content or attach images while using inline <code>/plan</code> arguments.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex enters plan mode and uses your optional inline prompt as the first planning request.</p> <p>While Codex is already working, <code>/plan</code> is temporarily unavailable.</p> <h3 id=\"set-or-view-a-task-goal-with-goal\">Set or view a task goal with <code>/goal</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/goal &lt;objective&gt;</code> to set the goal, for example <code>/goal Finish the migration and keep tests green</code>.</li> <li>Type <code>/goal</code> to view the current goal.</li> <li>Use <code>/goal edit</code> to revise the objective. Use <code>/goal pause</code>, <code>/goal resume</code>, or <code>/goal clear</code> to pause, resume, or remove it.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex keeps the goal attached to the active chat while work continues.</p> <p>Goal objectives must be non-empty and at most 4,000 characters. For longer instructions, put the details in a file and point the goal at that file.</p> <h3 id=\"toggle-experimental-features-with-experimental\">Toggle experimental features with <code>/experimental</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/experimental</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>Toggle the features you want (for example, Network proxy or Prevent sleep while running), then restart Codex if the prompt asks you to.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex saves your feature choices to config and applies them on restart.</p> <h3 id=\"approve-an-auto-review-denial-with-approve\">Approve an auto review denial with <code>/approve</code></h3> <p>Use <code>/approve</code> when the automatic reviewer denied a recent action and you want Codex to retry it once.</p> <ol> <li>Type <code>/approve</code>.</li> <li>Confirm the retry when Codex shows the relevant denied action.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex retries that denied action once under the current session policy.</p> <h3 id=\"configure-memories-with-memories\">Configure memories with <code>/memories</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/memories</code>.</li> <li>Choose whether Codex should use existing memories, generate new memories, or keep memory behavior disabled.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex updates the relevant memory settings for future sessions.</p> <h3 id=\"use-skills-with-skills\">Use skills with <code>/skills</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/skills</code>.</li> <li>Pick the skill you want Codex to apply.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex inserts the selected skill context so the next request follows that skill's instructions.</p> <p><a id=\"import-claude-code-configuration-with-import\"></a> <a id=\"import-claude-code-setup-with-import\"></a> <a id=\"cli-import-claude-code-setup-with-import\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"import-claude-code-or-cursor-setup-with-import\">Import Claude Code or Cursor setup with <code>/import</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/import</code>.</li> <li>Choose <strong>Claude Code</strong> or <strong>Cursor</strong>.</li> <li>Select the setup, project files, or recent chats you want to migrate.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex opens the external-agent import picker and imports the selected supported artifacts into Codex configuration and local files. Session discovery includes up to 50 chats from the last 30 days.</p> <p>Run <code>/import</code> from a local TUI session. It's unavailable while a task is running, in remote sessions, and while connected to the local app-server daemon.</p> <p>For the desktop app workflow and supported artifact types, see <a href=\"#/article/a-2b09a0f3c8670621\">Import from another agent</a>.</p> <p><a id=\"clear-the-terminal-and-start-a-new-chat-with-clear\"></a> <a id=\"clear-the-terminal-and-start-a-new-task-with-clear\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"clear-the-terminal-and-start-a-new-chat-with-clear\">Clear the terminal and start a new chat with <code>/clear</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/clear</code> and press Enter.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex clears the terminal, resets the visible transcript, and starts a fresh chat in the same CLI session.</p> <p>To name the new chat as you create it, run <code>/clear release prep</code>.</p> <p>Unlike <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>L</kbd>, <code>/clear</code> starts a new chat.</p> <p><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>L</kbd> only clears the terminal view and keeps the current chat. Codex disables both actions while a task is in progress.</p> <h3 id=\"archive-the-current-session-with-archive\">Archive the current session with <code>/archive</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/archive</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>Confirm that you want to archive the current session.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex archives the session and returns to the command center when connected to a local background server or remote server. Without a shared server, Codex exits. Codex keeps the transcript; restore it later with <code>codex unarchive &lt;SESSION&gt;</code>.</p> <p>If a turn is running, confirming <code>/archive</code> stops that turn before archiving.</p> <h3 id=\"delete-the-current-session-with-delete\">Delete the current session with <code>/delete</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/delete</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>Confirm that you want to delete the current session.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex permanently deletes the transcript and spawned descendant sessions. When connected to a local background server or remote server, Codex returns to the command center. Without a shared server, Codex exits.</p> <p><code>/delete</code> is unavailable while a chat is running or in a side chat.</p> <h3 id=\"update-permissions-with-permissions\">Update permissions with <code>/permissions</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/permissions</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>Select the approval preset that matches your comfort level, for example <code>Auto</code> for hands-off runs or <code>Read Only</code> to review edits. When named permission profiles are active, the picker also shows configured custom profiles and their descriptions.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex announces the updated policy. Future actions respect the updated approval mode until you change it again.</p> <h3 id=\"include-ide-context-with-ide\">Include IDE context with <code>/ide</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/ide</code>.</li> <li>Add optional inline text if you want to explain what Codex should do with the current IDE selection or open files.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex includes available IDE context in the next prompt.</p> <h3 id=\"toggle-vim-mode-with-vim\">Toggle Vim mode with <code>/vim</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/vim</code>.</li> <li>Continue editing in the composer.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex toggles composer Vim mode for the current session. To make Vim mode the default for new sessions, set <code>tui.vim_mode_default = true</code> in <code>config.toml</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"set-up-the-elevated-windows-sandbox-with-setup-default-sandbox\">Set up the elevated Windows sandbox with <code>/setup-default-sandbox</code></h3> <p>This command appears only on Windows when Codex is using the degraded restricted-token sandbox.</p> <ol> <li>Type <code>/setup-default-sandbox</code>.</li> <li>Follow the administrator setup flow.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex configures the elevated Windows sandbox and selects the corresponding automatic approval preset.</p> <h3 id=\"copy-the-latest-response-with-copy\">Copy the latest response with <code>/copy</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/copy</code> and press Enter.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex copies the latest completed Codex output to your clipboard.</p> <p>If a turn is still running, <code>/copy</code> uses the latest completed output instead of the in-progress response. The command is unavailable before the first completed Codex output and immediately after a rollback.</p> <p>You can also press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>O</kbd> from the main TUI to copy the latest completed response without opening the slash command menu.</p> <h3 id=\"toggle-raw-scrollback-with-raw\">Toggle raw scrollback with <code>/raw</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/raw</code>, <code>/raw on</code>, or <code>/raw off</code>.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex toggles raw scrollback mode, which makes terminal selection and copying more direct. You can also use the default <kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>R</kbd> binding or persist the default with <code>tui.raw_output_mode = true</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"inspect-the-session-with-status\">Inspect the session with <code>/status</code></h3> <ol> <li>In any chat, type <code>/status</code>.</li> <li>Review the output for the active model, approval policy, writable roots, and current token usage. When the TUI connects remotely, the output also shows the remote address and the server version.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex prints a summary confirming that it's operating where you expect.</p> <h3 id=\"view-account-usage-with-usage\">View account usage with <code>/usage</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/usage</code> to open the usage menu.</li> <li>Choose whether to show token activity or redeem an available earned reset.</li> <li>To open token activity directly, type <code>/usage daily</code>, <code>/usage weekly</code>, or <code>/usage cumulative</code>.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex opens usage actions or shows account token activity for the selected view. If the session doesn't have Codex service account auth, Codex shows a sign-in requirement.</p> <h3 id=\"inspect-config-layers-with-debug-config\">Inspect config layers with <code>/debug-config</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/debug-config</code>.</li> <li>Review the output for config layer order (lowest precedence first), on/off state, and policy sources.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex prints layer diagnostics plus policy details such as <code>allowed_approval_policies</code>, <code>allowed_sandbox_modes</code>, <code>mcp_servers</code>, <code>rules</code>, and <code>experimental_network</code> when configured.</p> <p>Use this output to debug why an effective setting differs from <code>config.toml</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"configure-footer-items-with-statusline\">Configure footer items with <code>/statusline</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/statusline</code>.</li> <li>Use the picker to toggle and reorder items, then confirm.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: The footer status line updates immediately and persists to <code>tui.status_line</code> in <code>config.toml</code>.</p> <p>Available status-line items include model, model+reasoning, context stats, rate limits, git branch, token counters, session id, current directory/project root, and Codex version.</p> <h3 id=\"configure-terminal-title-items-with-title\">Configure terminal title items with <code>/title</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/title</code>.</li> <li>Use the picker to toggle and reorder items, then confirm.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: The terminal window or tab title updates immediately and persists to <code>tui.terminal_title</code> in <code>config.toml</code>.</p> <p>Available title items include app name, project, spinner, status, thread, git branch, model, and task progress.</p> <h3 id=\"choose-a-syntax-theme-with-theme\">Choose a syntax theme with <code>/theme</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/theme</code>.</li> <li>Preview a theme from the picker, then confirm.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex updates syntax highlighting and persists the choice to <code>tui.theme</code> in <code>config.toml</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"choose-a-terminal-pet-with-pets\">Choose a terminal pet with <code>/pets</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/pets</code> (or <code>/pet</code>) to open the pet picker.</li> <li>Choose a built-in or custom pet, or turn pets off.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex displays the selected ambient pet in supported terminals and persists the selection. You can also type <code>/pets off</code> to hide it.</p> <h3 id=\"remap-tui-shortcuts-with-keymap\">Remap TUI shortcuts with <code>/keymap</code></h3> <p>Use <code>/keymap</code> to inspect, update, and persist keyboard shortcut bindings for the TUI.</p> <ol> <li>Type <code>/keymap</code>.</li> <li>Pick the shortcut context and action you want to change.</li> <li>Enter the new binding or remove the existing one.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex updates the active keymap and writes the custom binding to <code>tui.keymap</code> in <code>config.toml</code>.</p> <p>Key bindings use names such as <code>ctrl-a</code>, <code>shift-enter</code>, and <code>page-down</code>. Context-specific bindings override <code>tui.keymap.global</code>; an empty binding list unbinds the action.</p> <h3 id=\"check-background-terminals-with-ps\">Check background terminals with <code>/ps</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/ps</code>.</li> <li>Review the list of background terminals and their status.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex shows each background terminal's command plus up to three recent, non-empty output lines so you can gauge progress at a glance.</p> <p>Background terminals appear when <code>unified_exec</code> is in use; otherwise, the list may be empty.</p> <h3 id=\"stop-background-terminals-with-stop\">Stop background terminals with <code>/stop</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/stop</code>.</li> <li>Confirm if Codex asks before stopping the listed terminals.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex stops all background terminals for the current session. <code>/clean</code> is still available as an alias for <code>/stop</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"keep-transcripts-lean-with-compact\">Keep transcripts lean with <code>/compact</code></h3> <ol> <li>After a long exchange, type <code>/compact</code>.</li> <li>Confirm when Codex offers to summarize the chat so far.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex replaces earlier turns with a concise summary, freeing context while keeping critical details.</p> <h3 id=\"review-changes-with-diff\">Review changes with <code>/diff</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/diff</code> to inspect the Git diff.</li> <li>Scroll through the output inside the CLI to review edits and added files.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex shows changes you've staged, changes you haven't staged yet, and files Git hasn't started tracking, so you can decide what to keep.</p> <h3 id=\"highlight-files-with-mention\">Highlight files with <code>/mention</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/mention</code> followed by a path, for example <code>/mention src/lib/api.ts</code>.</li> <li>Select the matching result from the popup.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex adds the file to the chat, ensuring follow-up turns reference it directly.</p> <p><a id=\"start-a-new-conversation-with-new\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"start-a-new-chat-with-new\">Start a new chat with <code>/new</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/new</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>If Codex offers a checkout choice, choose the current directory or a new worktree.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex starts a fresh chat in the same CLI session, so you can switch chats without leaving your terminal.</p> <p>To name the new chat as you create it, run <code>/new bug bash</code>.</p> <p>Unlike <code>/clear</code>, <code>/new</code> doesn't clear the current terminal view first.</p> <p><a id=\"rename-the-current-chat-with-rename\"></a> <a id=\"rename-the-current-task-with-rename\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"rename-the-current-chat-with-rename\">Rename the current chat with <code>/rename</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/rename &lt;name&gt;</code>, or type <code>/rename</code> to open the naming prompt.</li> <li>Enter a short name that will help you find the chat later.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex updates the saved chat name without changing its transcript.</p> <p><a id=\"resume-a-saved-conversation-with-resume\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"resume-a-saved-chat-with-resume\">Resume a saved chat with <code>/resume</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/resume</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>Choose the session you want from the saved-session picker.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex reloads the selected chat's transcript so you can pick up where you left off, keeping the original history intact.</p> <p><a id=\"fork-the-current-conversation-with-fork\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"fork-the-current-chat-with-fork\">Fork the current chat with <code>/fork</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/fork</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>If Codex offers a checkout choice, choose the current directory or a new worktree.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex clones the current chat into a new chat with a fresh ID, leaving the original transcript untouched so you can explore an alternative approach in parallel.</p> <p>If you need to fork a saved session instead of the current one, run <code>codex fork</code> in your terminal to open the session picker.</p> <h3 id=\"continue-in-the-desktop-app-with-app\">Continue in the desktop app with <code>/app</code></h3> <p>On macOS and Windows, type <code>/app</code> to open the current session in the ChatGPT desktop app. If the app isn't installed or running, Codex shows an error asking you to install or launch it.</p> <p>Expected: The desktop app opens the same saved chat so you can continue there.</p> <p><a id=\"start-a-side-conversation-with-side\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"start-a-side-chat-with-side\">Start a side chat with <code>/side</code></h3> <p>Use <code>/side</code> to start an ephemeral fork from the current chat without switching away from the main chat.</p> <ol> <li>Type <code>/side</code> to open a side chat.</li> <li>Optionally add inline text, for example <code>/side Check whether this plan has an obvious risk</code>.</li> <li>Return to the parent chat after the focused detour finishes.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex opens a side chat whose transcript is separate from the parent chat. While you are in side mode, the TUI continues to show the parent chat's status so you can see whether the main chat is still running.</p> <p><code>/side</code> is unavailable inside another side chat and during review mode.</p> <h3 id=\"generate-agentsmd-with-init\">Generate <code>AGENTS.md</code> with <code>/init</code></h3> <ol> <li>Run <code>/init</code> in the directory where you want Codex to look for persistent instructions.</li> <li>Review the generated <code>AGENTS.md</code>, then edit it to match your repository conventions.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex creates an <code>AGENTS.md</code> scaffold you can refine and commit for future sessions.</p> <h3 id=\"ask-for-a-working-tree-review-with-review\">Ask for a working tree review with <code>/review</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/review</code>.</li> <li>Follow up with <code>/diff</code> if you want to inspect the exact file changes.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex summarizes issues it finds in your working tree, focusing on behavior changes and missing tests. It uses the current session model unless you set <code>review_model</code> in <code>config.toml</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"list-mcp-tools-with-mcp\">List MCP tools with <code>/mcp</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/mcp</code>.</li> <li>Review the list to confirm which MCP servers and tools are available.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: You see the configured Model Context Protocol (MCP) tools Codex can call in this session.</p> <p>Use <code>/mcp verbose</code> to include detailed server diagnostics. Use <code>/mcp login &lt;name&gt;</code> to sign in to a configured MCP server from the active session.</p> <h3 id=\"browse-apps-with-apps\">Browse apps with <code>/apps</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/apps</code>.</li> <li>Pick an app from the list.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex inserts the app mention into the composer as <code>$app-slug</code>, so you can immediately ask Codex to use it.</p> <h3 id=\"browse-plugins-with-plugins\">Browse plugins with <code>/plugins</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/plugins</code>.</li> <li>Choose a marketplace tab, then pick a plugin to inspect its capabilities or available actions.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex opens the plugin browser so you can review installed plugins, discoverable plugins that your configuration allows, and installed plugin state. Press <kbd>Space</kbd> on an installed plugin to toggle its enabled state.</p> <h3 id=\"view-and-manage-lifecycle-hooks-with-hooks\">View and manage lifecycle hooks with <code>/hooks</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/hooks</code>.</li> <li>Choose a hook event to inspect the matching handlers.</li> <li>Trust, disable, or re-enable non-managed hooks as needed.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex opens the hook browser so you can review configured lifecycle hooks. Managed hooks appear as managed and can't be disabled from the user hook browser.</p> <h3 id=\"manage-chats-with-agents\">Manage chats with <code>/agents</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/agents</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>Select a chat from the command center to open it.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex shows an overview of chats on the connected server. You can inspect their status and switch between them. To open the command center directly from your terminal, run <code>codex agents</code>. The command center requires a shared local or remote server.</p> <p><a id=\"switch-agent-threads-with-agent\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"switch-agent-threads-with-subagents\">Switch agent threads with <code>/subagents</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/subagents</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>Select the thread you want from the picker.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex switches the active thread so you can inspect or continue that agent's work.</p> <h3 id=\"send-feedback-with-feedback\">Send feedback with <code>/feedback</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/feedback</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>Follow the prompts to include logs or diagnostics.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex collects the requested diagnostics and submits them to the maintainers.</p> <h3 id=\"sign-out-with-logout\">Sign out with <code>/logout</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/logout</code> and press Enter.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex clears local credentials for the current user session.</p> <h3 id=\"exit-the-cli-with-quit-or-exit\">Exit the CLI with <code>/quit</code> or <code>/exit</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/quit</code> (or <code>/exit</code>) and press Enter.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex exits immediately. Save or commit any important work first.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Use these commands to control Codex from the VS Code Command Palette. You can also bind them to keyboard shortcuts.</p> <h2 id=\"assign-a-key-binding\">Assign a key binding</h2> <p>To assign or change a key binding for a Codex command:</p> <ol> <li>Open the Command Palette (<strong>Cmd+Shift+P</strong> on macOS or <strong>Ctrl+Shift+P</strong> on Windows/Linux).</li> <li>Run <strong>Preferences: Open Keyboard Shortcuts</strong>.</li> <li>Search for <code>Codex</code> or the command ID (for example, <code>chatgpt.newChat</code>).</li> <li>Select the pencil icon, then enter the shortcut you want.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"extension-commands\">Extension commands</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Command</th> <th>Default key binding</th> <th>Description</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.addToThread</code></td> <td>-</td> <td>Add selected text range as context for the current chat</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.addFileToThread</code></td> <td>-</td> <td>Add the entire file as context for the current chat</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.newChat</code></td> <td>macOS: <code>Cmd+N</code><br>Windows/Linux: <code>Ctrl+N</code></td> <td>Create a new chat</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.newCodexPanel</code></td> <td>-</td> <td>Create a new Codex panel</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.openCommandMenu</code></td> <td>-</td> <td>Open the Codex command menu</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>chatgpt.openSidebar</code></td> <td>-</td> <td>Open the Codex sidebar panel</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Slash commands let you control Codex without leaving the composer. Use them to check status, switch between local and cloud mode, or send feedback.</p> <h2 id=\"use-a-slash-command\">Use a slash command</h2> <ol> <li>In the Codex composer, type <code>/</code>.</li> <li>Select a command from the list, or keep typing to filter (for example, <code>/status</code>).</li> <li>Press <strong>Enter</strong>.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"available-slash-commands\">Available slash commands</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Slash command</th> <th>Description</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>/approve</code></td> <td>Approve one retry of a recent automatic-review denial, when automatic review is active.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/cloud</code></td> <td>Run the chat in the cloud, when cloud execution is available.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/cloud-environment</code></td> <td>Choose the cloud environment for the chat.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/compact</code></td> <td>Compact the current chat's context.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/fast</code></td> <td>Turn a catalog-provided Fast service tier on or off, when available.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/feedback</code></td> <td>Open the feedback dialog to submit feedback and optionally include logs.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/fork</code></td> <td>Copy a local chat into a new local chat.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/goal</code></td> <td>Set a persistent goal for Codex to work toward.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/ide-context</code></td> <td>Turn automatic IDE context on or off.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/init</code></td> <td>Generate an <code>AGENTS.md</code> scaffold for the current project.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/local</code></td> <td>Run the chat in your local workspace.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/mcp</code></td> <td>Open MCP status to view connected servers.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/memories</code></td> <td>Configure whether the chat can use or generate memories, when Memories is available.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/model</code></td> <td>Choose the model for the current chat.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/personality</code></td> <td>Choose how Codex responds, when the current model supports personalities.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/plan</code></td> <td>Toggle plan mode for multi-step planning.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/project</code></td> <td>Choose a project for new chats.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/reasoning</code></td> <td>Choose the reasoning effort for the current chat.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/review</code></td> <td>Start code review mode to review uncommitted changes or compare against a base branch.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/side</code></td> <td>Start a temporary side chat without interrupting the main chat.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/status</code></td> <td>Show the chat ID, context usage, and rate limits.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>/worktree</code></td> <td>Run the chat in a new Git worktree.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table>"};
